        "h": "Register — the shared chapter, now fully spent, and what is not in it",
        "body": "### ⚠️ One book chapter, three app chapters — and this is the last claimant\n|**Printed**|**Content**|**Written in**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**193**|background, prevalence, the DSM-5 three-way split, the comorbidity note, list I|**here** — `ax-1`, `ax-2`|\n|**194 top**|lists II and III|**`ps-ocd`** *(and cited in `ax-2` for the taxonomy only)*|\n|**194 bottom**|GAD criteria and the suicide note|**here** — `ax-3`|\n|**195 · 196**|WATCHERS, specific phobia, social phobia; panic disorder, the cycle figure, STUDENTS FEAR the 3Cs|**here** — `ax-3`, `ax-4`, `ax-5`|\n|**197 top**|agoraphobia and its note box|**here** — `ax-4`, `ax-1`|\n|**197 bottom · 198**|OCD criteria; the all-figure OCD page|**`ps-ocd`**|\n|**199 top**|PTSD, ASD, the TRAUMA mnemonic|**`ps-ptsd`**|\n|**199 bottom**|the shared differential diagnosis|**`ps-ocd`'s `oc-6`** — pointed at from `ax-6`, not repeated|\n|**200 · 201**|investigations, prognosis, the whole of treatment|**here** — `ax-7`, `ax-8`, `ax-9`|\n\n- **✅ The chapter is spent:** every page of Psychiatry ch.3 is **now written somewhere**. Nothing is left owed to a fourth chapter, and no row is filed **out** of this one.\n- **⚠️ Three lines spent first, by `oc-8`:** the **4-12 weeks for OCD**, the **12-month minimum** and **clomipramine for OCD**. All three are printed on 200-201, and are stated here as the **general rule** they belong to while `oc-8` works them for OCD. **The spine's owner using its own spine, not a second copy.**\n\n### ⚠️ Rows filed IN, and audited against the source\n- **`sy-10` filed a whole lecture block here:** `ps-symptom` deferred the **ENTIRE ANXIETY HALF of `L4,5`** — a lecture block, the largest single row in the module's register. **Paid in full, and here is where each piece landed:**\n\n|**What `sy-10` deferred**|**Paid in**|\n|---|---|\n|prevalence and impact; illness not weakness|`ax-1`|\n|the three measures of *excessive* — change, prolonged duration, QOL|`ax-1`|\n|intact insight, no psychotic features|`ax-1`|\n|the DSM list|`ax-2`|\n|the differential|`ax-6`|\n|assessment, and **NO DIAGNOSTIC TEST**|`ax-6`|\n|CBT; 2-6 weeks; one year then gradual withdrawal; not addictive|`ax-8`|\n|hospitalisation usually unnecessary; ECT not effective; SSRIs, SNRIs/TCAs, benzodiazepines|`ax-9`|\n\n- **⚠️ `sy-10` was right, the plan wrong:** `theory-plan.md` recorded the book as this chapter's only source and gave `L4,5` wholly to `ps-symptom`. **It has a deck too** — but that half measures **233 words**, so **the book carries the chapter almost single-handed**. ⚠️ **A deck existing and a deck being a source are different claims.**\n\n- **⚠️ Four divergences:** the deck and the book differ over the psychotherapy named, the onset figure, the addiction caveat and ECT. **Each is recorded where it is used**, three in `ax-8` and one in `ax-9`, and **none is corrected**: three are a narrower source against a flatter one, and the fourth is two numbers for one thing.\n\n### What these sources do not contain\n- **⚠️ No dose, unit or route for any drug**, in either source. Supplied and tagged in `ax-9`.\n- **⚠️ Nine disorders named and never taught** across the three lists; the four in list I are answered and tagged in `ax-2`.\n- **No ICD-11 anywhere** — the same finding `oc-10` records for the OCD deck.\n- **⚠️ Three anxiolytics absent:** **no buspirone, no hydroxyzine, no pregabalin** — three drugs used in generalized anxiety. **buspirone and hydroxyzine return ZERO** across the book chapter and all 25 decks; **pregabalin returns exactly ONE hit, and it is not this** — `L8) Cranial nerves`, in the **trigeminal neuralgia** drug list, which is `nr-cranial`'s. *(Recorded, not supplied — the chapter's drug list stays the book's.)*\n- **No acute management of a panic attack.** Neither source says what to do **during** one; `ps-psychoed`'s `pe-2` gets closest with *finding a safe space reduces risk*.\n- **No per-disorder epidemiology** — one range, **2-13 %**, for the whole category, and one sex ratio.\n- **No neurobiology.** Aetiology is **one sentence** — genetic predisposition interacting with stressors — where `ps-ocd`'s `oc-4` has four causal groups and a circuit.\n- **No prognosis figures** — *most cases show significant improvement* is the whole of it.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.3 printed pp. 193-201, read end to end; the page-split table at the foot of content\\neuro\\book\\psych-ch03-anxiety.txt; L4,5 back half; `ps-symptom`'s `sy-10`, `ps-ocd`'s `oc-6`, `oc-8` and `oc-10`, and `ps-ptsd`'s `pt-4` for the register audit. The 233-word deck measurement and the buspirone/hydroxyzine/pregabalin zero-return grep were run at the hub on 2026-08-23",
