        "id": "sz-6",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "The DSM-5 criteria",
        "body": "### Criterion A — characteristic symptoms\n- **TWO OR MORE** of the following, each present for a significant portion of time during a **1-MONTH period** *(or less if successfully treated)* —\n  - **1. Delusions**\n  - **2. Hallucinations**\n  - **3. Disorganized speech** — e.g. frequent **derailment** or **incoherence**\n  - **4.** Grossly disorganized or **CATATONIC behaviour**\n  - **5. Negative symptoms** — **affective flattening**, **alogia**, **avolition**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ The note box — when ONE symptom is enough\n- **Only ONE criterion A symptom is required if:** the **delusions are BIZARRE**, **or** the hallucinations are **a voice keeping up a RUNNING COMMENTARY** on the person's behaviour or thoughts, **or** **TWO OR MORE VOICES CONVERSING** with each other.\n- **⚠️ This is where Schneider survives.** Every item in that box is a first-rank symptom from `sz-5`. **The single most examinable sentence on the page.**\n\n### The remaining criteria, as the book letters them\n|**Criterion**|**What it requires**|\n|---|---|\n|**A** *(second one — see the defect below)*|**Onset of the disturbance:** one or more **major areas of functioning** — work, interpersonal relations, self-care — **markedly below the level achieved prior to onset**. In childhood or adolescent onset, **failure to ACHIEVE the expected level**|\n|**B — Duration**|continuous signs for **AT LEAST 6 MONTHS**, which **must include at least 1 MONTH of criterion A symptoms** *(or less if successfully treated)*. The rest may be **prodromal or residual**, shown as **only negative symptoms** or as criterion A symptoms in **ATTENUATED form** — odd beliefs, unusual perceptual experiences|\n|**C — Schizoaffective and mood exclusion**|ruled out because **no major depressive or manic episode occurred concurrently** with active-phase symptoms; **or**, if mood episodes did occur, their **total duration was BRIEF relative** to the active and residual periods|\n|**D — Substance / medical exclusion**|not due to the **direct physiological effects of a substance** (drug of abuse, medication) **or a medical condition**|\n\n- **⚠️ Two durations, two tests:** **1 month** of active symptoms sits **inside** **6 months** of continuous disturbance. **Answering *one month* to a duration question is wrong unless the question asks about criterion A.**\n- **⚠️ LETTERING DEFECT, recorded not corrected:** **the book prints A, A, B, C, D.** The functioning criterion restarts at **A** after the note box, so every later letter is shifted by one against standard DSM-5. **The content is right; only the labels are off.**\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7 printed p.232 — Diagnostic Criteria for Schizophrenia (DSM-5), the note box, and the criteria as lettered on the page",
        "qs": []
