        "h": "Positive and negative symptoms",
        "body": "|**Feature**|**POSITIVE**|**NEGATIVE (deficit)**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**What they are**|things **most individuals do NOT normally experience** but that are **present** — the **manifestations of PSYCHOSIS**|**DEFICITS** of normal emotional responses or thought processes|\n|**Include**|**delusions** · **disordered thoughts and speech** · **hallucinations** — tactile, auditory, visual, olfactory, gustatory, and **typically related to the content of the delusional theme**|**flat expressions** (little emotion) · **poverty of speech (ALOGIA)** · **inability to experience pleasure (ANHEDONIA)** · **lack of desire to form relationships** · **lack of motivation (AVOLITION)**|\n|**⚠️ Response to medication**|**responds WELL**|**often LIMITED**|\n|**Burden**|—|**contribute MORE to poor quality of life**, functional ability and **burden on others**|\n|**Association**|—|often linked to a history of **POOR ADJUSTMENT BEFORE ONSET**|\n\n- **⚠️ The asymmetry is the point.** The symptoms that **respond to treatment** are not the symptoms that **cause the disability**. That is why a patient can be free of voices and still unemployable, and it is why the prognosis table in `ps-schizmgmt` puts **negative symptoms** on the poor side and **positive symptoms** on the good side.\n- **⚠️ Content tracks the delusion:** the book says so in one clause, and it is the reason a persecutory delusion and derogatory voices arrive together in four of the five cases in `ps-schizmgmt`.\n- **Poverty of speech** is one of the three terms `ps-symptom`'s `sy-10` records as **returning zero across all 25 decks** and supplying. **The book prints it here**, so the supply is now corroborated by the material.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7 printed p.233 — Positive and Negative (deficit) symptoms, down to the end of that section",
