        "h": "Register — the split, what goes to `ps-schizmgmt`, and what is not here",
        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, forecast before writing\n- **Why:** book Psychiatry ch.7 runs to **4,075 body words over eleven printed pages** — **more source than any single chapter in this module has been written from**. At the module's measured **281-343 w/pp** and its measured **150-200 % inflation**, one chapter forecasts at **20-30 pp**, two to three times the **≤13 hard shape**. **No trim reaches that**, so it was split **before** writing — the second forecast split in the module, after `nr-movement`/`nr-epilepsy`.\n- **⚠️ The deck does not rescue it:** `L11,12` is **2,251 words of which 1,933 — 86 % — are FIVE CASE VIGNETTES**. Its **teaching content is about 320 words**. **A deck word count is not a teaching word count**, and this is the widest gap between the two yet measured in the project.\n- **The seam:** **`Course & Prognosis` on printed 233** — contiguous in the book, needing **no reordering**, and it divides the source almost evenly: **2,131 words here**, **1,944 to `ps-schizmgmt`**.\n- **Neither half carries a question**, so nothing moves; `ps-psychosis` keeps its id and **`SCHEDULE` is untouched**.\n\n### ⚠️ Register (§14.5) — filed OUT to `ps-schizmgmt`\n|**Deferred**|**Where it is printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Course and prognosis**, and the whole **thirteen-row good-vs-poor prognosis poster**|printed 233 lower - 234|\n|**Investigations**|printed 234|\n|**Differential diagnosis**, psychiatric and organic|printed 235|\n|**Treatment**, and the **entire ANTIPSYCHOTIC block** — three classes, receptor mechanisms, the adverse-effect taxonomy, EPS treatment, clozapine and agranulocytosis, depot preparations|printed 235-238|\n|**Hospitalisation indications** · **ECT indications** · **psychotherapy**|deck `L11,12` + printed 238|\n|**All five case vignettes and their unanswered questions**|deck `L11,12`|\n\n- **⚠️ `ps-pharm` is paid elsewhere:** by `ps-schizmgmt`, not here. Book Psych ch.11 heads **`Antipsychotics`**, teaches indications as a picture, then defers everything else in one line — ***Classes, mechanism of action & adverse effect: (See 'schizophrenia' lecture)***. **That deferred content is printed 236-238**, and it belongs to the management half. **`ps-pharm` must point at it, not repeat it.**\n- **Filed IN to this chapter:** **`ps-symptom`'s `sy-10`** deferred **thought insertion, withdrawal, broadcasting and delusions of reference in full** to `ps-psychosis`. ⚠️ **`sy-6` already defines all four**, so what was owed was the *disorder* context, not the definitions — **paid in `sz-5`, which points at `sy-6` rather than restating it.**\n\n### What these sources do not contain\n- **⚠️ NO ICD-10 CRITERIA**, though ICD-10 is named twice as a diagnostic standard (`sz-4`).\n- **⚠️ No description of any subtype** — five named, none described; supplied and tagged in `sz-8`.\n- **⚠️ One theory under a plural heading:** `Biological Theories`, in `sz-3`; the glutamate and neurodevelopmental hypotheses exist only as poster boxes.\n- **No structural pathology in prose** — ventricles, grey matter, connectivity and NMDA hypofunction are **poster-only** (`sz-2`).\n- **No age-specific or paediatric presentation**, and **no perinatal or postpartum psychosis**.\n- **⚠️ Four psychotic disorders undefined:** **schizoaffective**, **schizophreniform**, **brief psychotic** and **delusional disorder** — all four are excluded by criterion C or the differential without being defined. **`ps-schizmgmt`'s differential is where the book comes closest.**\n- **⚠️ The retitle, and why:** the book chapter is *Schizophrenia* and the app chapter was *Approach to Psychosis*. **Neither source teaches an approach to psychosis in general** — both teach schizophrenia. The chapter is retitled to say so.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7 printed pp. 228-233, read end to end; L11,12, read end to end; the deferral to ch.11 is quoted from printed p.263 of the same book, cached in content\\neuro\\book\\psych-ch11-treatment.txt. Word counts measured at the hub 2026-08-23",
