        "body": "- **There are NO SPECIFIC INVESTIGATIONS — for schizophrenia.** The book says so in four words, and everything below is done for a reason other than making the diagnosis.\n- **Three purposes — and they are the whole section:**\n  - **exclude ORGANICITY**\n  - **monitor the general health state**\n  - **choose the medication — and monitor its side effects**\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ NOT ONE TEST IS NAMED.** No CBC, no imaging, no drug screen, no metabolic panel, no prolactin. **This is the chapter's clearest heading-without-a-body**, and unlike the ECT line it is not deferred anywhere either.\n- **⚠️⚠️ And it collides — with the chapter's own prescribing.** Printed 238 prescribes **clozapine** and warns of **AGRANULOCYTOSIS** — and **no monitoring parameter of any kind is printed in these eleven pages**, so the chapter never says to check a white cell count. *(The monitoring itself is supplied in `sm-8`, tagged.)*\n- **⚠️ `Exclude organicity`:** the same instruction as **`ps-symptom`'s `sy-9`**, which is the module's fullest treatment of it. **The differential in `sm-4` is what that exclusion actually looks like.**\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7 printed p.234 — Investigations, quoted in full; the clozapine and agranulocytosis lines are printed p.238",
