        "h": "The deck is five cases — and it prints no answers",
        "body": "- **⚠️⚠️ 1,933 of the deck's 2,251 words — 86 % — are these five vignettes.** They are the lecture's real content, they carry **full mental state examinations**, and **the deck asks nine questions across them and answers none.** Worked below from the criteria in `sz-6` and the differential in `sm-4`; **the workings are not printed by the deck**, and where a point comes from outside both sources it is tagged.\n\n|**#**|**The presentation**|**⚠️ What it is testing**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1**|**21 y, found sitting in the middle of traffic** — *the voices told me to do it*. **One year** of *people are not who they say they are*; **dropped out of school**, isolated. **Two or three voices commenting to each other on his behaviour.** Past marijuana, stopped 6 months ago because **it helped the voices**. MSE: dishevelled, **paces with his back to the wall**, **affect flat but congruent**, **tangential with loose associations**|**criterion A by the NOTE BOX ALONE** — voices conversing. **Duration is met at one year.** ⚠️ *Marijuana helped the voices* is the substance-exclusion trap: **he self-medicated, he was not intoxicated**|\n|**2**|**24 y, fight after feeling watched**; refuses an X-ray because **a machine lets the government into his head**. **Running commentary on his THOUGHTS**, **thought broadcast**, **thought withdrawal**; **neologisms**; **unclear about time**|**FIRST-RANK SYMPTOMS**, three of them (`sz-5`), and **running commentary is the second note-box shortcut**. ⚠️ **Disorientation in time is the organic alarm** — `sm-4`|\n|**3**|**21 y, few DAYS of persecutory and grandiose delusions**, command hallucinations to kill, **carrying a knife**; music festival **6 weeks ago** where friends used cannabis and Ecstasy; **labile, overactive, rapid speech**, **disoriented in time and place**, **poor short-term memory**|⚠️ **NOT schizophrenia — the duration fails.** Days, not the **1 month** of criterion A. **Substance-induced psychosis** and **brief psychotic disorder** lead the differential, with **bipolar mania** behind them on the lability and overactivity. ⚠️ **Command hallucinations plus a weapon is the admission decision**|\n|**4**|**23 y salesman, 6 months** of a workplace conspiracy — **bugged flat**, **tapped phone**, **a dental filling as a transmitter**; **hears colleagues' comments across a showroom**; **reads meaning into the arrangement of price labels**; refuses examination; **mother does not think he is psychotic**|**Delusions of REFERENCE** (the price labels) beside persecution, plus auditory hallucinations. ⚠️ **The insight problem is the management problem**: he will accept help only on his own delusional terms. ⚠️ **This is the one case the deck asks NO question about**|\n|**5**|**26 y, known schizophrenia since 20.** Risperidone → relapse on stopping → **risperidone DEPOT >12 months, no response** → **olanzapine, no response, 3 stone weight gain** → aripiprazole, and **6 weeks of deterioration on it**. **Trip wires and newspapered windows**; **running commentary**; **speech coherent, no formal thought disorder**; **he acknowledges the illness**|⚠️ **TREATMENT-RESISTANT SCHIZOPHRENIA — this is the clozapine case** (`sm-8`). **The depot already excluded non-compliance**, which is what makes it resistance rather than relapse. ⚠️ **The 3-stone gain on olanzapine is `sm-7`'s weight-gain clause** arriving in a patient|\n\n- **⚠️ Case 3 is the one that catches people.** Four of the five vignettes are schizophrenia; **the third is not**, and it fails on **duration** — the criterion easiest to skip when the psychosis is florid. **Read the time course before the mental state.**\n- **⚠️ One finding, two meanings:** *voices conversing* in case 1 and *running commentary* in case 2 are both the **one-symptom shortcut**; **command hallucinations in case 3 are not a diagnostic shortcut at all** — they are a **risk** finding. `sz-5` makes the same point.\n- **⚠️ All five meet `sm-5`'s list:** cases 1, 3 and 4 on **danger or initial assessment**, case 2 on **initial assessment and deterioration**, case 5 on **initial assessment for the clozapine switch**. *(Applied, not printed.)*\n\nSrc: L11,12 — the five case vignettes and their mental state examinations, read end to end; the deck prints nine questions across cases 1, 2 and 3 and no answers, and prints no question at all on cases 4 and 5. Diagnoses are worked from the DSM-5 criteria on printed p.232 and the differential on printed p.235 of neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7; the readings marked *applied* are not printed in either source",
