        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, recorded\n- **Forecast before writing**, the second such in the module after `nr-movement`/`nr-epilepsy`. Book Psychiatry ch.7 is **4,075 body words over eleven printed pages** — more source than any single chapter in this module has been written from — and at **281-343 w/pp** one chapter forecast at **20-30 pp** against a **≤13 hard shape**.\n- **⚠️ The deck does not rescue it:** `L11,12` is **2,251 words of which 1,933 are five case vignettes**. Its **teaching content is about 320 words** — **the widest gap between a deck's word count and its teaching content yet measured**, and the reason `sm-9` is a section rather than a footnote.\n- **The seam:** **`Course & Prognosis` on printed 233**, contiguous and needing no reordering. **`ps-psychosis`** took printed 228 to 233-upper; **this chapter** takes 233-lower to 238. **Neither half has a question**, so nothing moved and **`SCHEDULE` is untouched**.\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ Filed OUT — the one `ps-pharm` has been waiting for\n- **The deferral, in one red line:** book Psychiatry ch.11 heads `Antipsychotics`, teaches indications as a picture, then defers the rest — ***Classes, mechanism of action & adverse effect: (See 'schizophrenia' lecture).*** **That deferred content is `sm-6` and `sm-7`.**\n- **⚠️ `ps-pharm` must POINT, not repeat.** Three classes, receptor mechanisms, the whole adverse-effect taxonomy, EPS treatment, clozapine with agranulocytosis and depot preparations are written here. **What `ps-pharm` still owns is `L17`'s own material** — an agent list naming **five typicals and six atypicals this chapter does not** — and everything non-antipsychotic.\n- **⚠️ The MAOI adverse-effect gap — in `ps-pharm` is NOT filled here.** *MAOI*, *monoamine oxidase*, *phenelzine* and *tyramine* **appear on none of these eleven pages**; this chapter is antipsychotics only. **That gap stays open.**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ Two things this chapter defers — AND BOTH ARE ALREADY CACHED\n|**What is missing here**|**Where I first said it lived**|**Where it ACTUALLY is**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**NEUROLEPTIC MALIGNANT SYNDROME** — named twice, described nowhere (`sm-5`, `sm-7`)|***(refer to psychiatric emergency)*** — **Psychiatry ch.10, printed 256-260**, recorded **NOT READ**|⚠️ **`L15` teaches it IN FULL** — tetrad, mortality **10-20 %**, incidence **0.02-3 %**, **2:1** male, age not a risk factor, mechanism, associated medications, seven labs, nine-step treatment — **and `L16` teaches it again.** `ps-emerg`'s, from the decks|\n|**ECT** beyond its indications (`sm-8`)|**no pointer is printed**; **Psychiatry ch.12**, printed 265-270, recorded **NOT READ**|⚠️ **`L18 Devices in Psychiatry` teaches ECT at length** — procedure, mechanism, indications, the stigma, cognitive effects, and rTMS/VNS/tDCS against it. `ps-devices`' deck, cached|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-23.** Both were recorded as **unread book chapters** on the strength of **the book’s own cross-reference**, without probing the twenty-five cached decks. **A grep would have closed both in a minute.** The standing rule — *read the slide before declaring a gap* — failed here in the one direction it is meant to catch. **Neither is filled here**, because each is another chapter’s core content; **but neither needs a render.**\n\n### ⚠️ Three divergences between the deck and the book\n|**Point**|**Deck**|**Book**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Outcome**|**thirds** — 1/3 recovery, 1/3 partial, 1/3 chronic|**four graded courses**, 22/35/8/38 (`sm-1`)|\n|**CBT**|listed as a psychotherapy, unqualified|**evidence is MINIMAL** (`sm-8`)|\n|**Prognostic predictors**|a **heading with a video link and no body**|**a thirteen-row poster** (`sm-2`)|\n\n- **✅ They agree exactly — on hospitalisation and on ECT indications** — the only two blocks in this chapter where both sources print the same list.\n\n### What these sources do not contain\n- **⚠️ No dose — for any of the SEVEN antipsychotics**; supplied and tagged in `sm-6`. **Route appears once, as depot against oral.**\n- **⚠️ No monitoring parameter of any kind** — the chapter prescribes clozapine, names agranulocytosis, and never asks for a white cell count (`sm-3`).\n- **⚠️ Not one investigation is named**, and **not one of the eleven medical differentials is expanded** (`sm-3`, `sm-4`).\n- **⚠️ Seven psychosocial modalities named — none described** (`sm-8`); **quetiapine named, never classified** (`sm-6`).\n- **No outcome figures: no relapse rate, no adherence rate and no remission figure** — the course table in `sm-1` is the whole of it, and it sums to 103 %.\n- **The chapter ends bare: no summary, no key-points box and no question set**, and — unlike Psychiatry ch.3 — **no further-reading list**.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.7 printed pp. 233-238, read end to end; L11,12, read end to end; the ch.11 deferral is quoted from printed p.263, cached in content\\neuro\\book\\psych-ch11-treatment.txt. Word counts and the deck's teaching-vs-case split were measured at the hub 2026-08-23",
