        "body": "|**Consideration**|**What is printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Pregnancy**|**avoidance of prescription is better unless highly needed.** ⚠️ ***Paroxetine is CLASS D***|\n|**Antidepressant-induced MANIA**|**more with TCAs, SSRIs, SNRIs and NaSSAs.** ⚠️ **Note box: NDRI (bupropion) usually does NOT induce mania**|\n|**SUICIDE**|**ALL antidepressants carry the risk** · highest **UNDER 25 YEARS** · highest within the **FIRST 6 MONTHS** of use · ratio **4-7 per 1000**|\n|**Sexual side effects**|**usually REVERSIBLE**|\n\n- **⚠️ The suicide block is four numbers — and every one is examinable:** **all** agents · **<25** · **first 6 months** · **4-7/1000**. **It is also the mechanism behind the four S's** in `ph-4` — *suicidal thoughts* is on that mnemonic for this reason.\n- **⚠️ Bupropion is the exception twice over.** It is the one antidepressant that **usually does not induce mania** and the one that **usually causes no sexual dysfunction** (`ph-4`) — and it is the only one carrying a **seizure risk**. **The class that touches dopamine behaves differently in three places.**\n- **⚠️ A firmer statement: lithium and sodium valproate are contraindicated in pregnancy and lactation** (`ph-8`) — **firmer than the antidepressants’ *avoid unless highly needed*.** Read the two together before answering a pregnancy question.\n\n### ⚠️ Two deck slides that say nothing\n- **The pregnancy slide, sl.15:** a **photograph of a positive pregnancy test and nothing else** — **no drug, no trimester rule, no recommendation**. The point was made verbally, and **the book's two lines above are the whole printed content.**\n- **⚠️ Slide 16 is two uncaptioned images** — a noose dissolving into birds, and a woman screaming with her hands over her ears — **sitting inside the *special considerations* run**. **Its intended point is NOT RECOVERABLE from the file.** Suicidality, a switch to mania and agitation are all plausible and **none is recorded as the answer.**\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.11 printed p.262 — considerations 2), 3), 4), 5) and the note box; L17 sl.15-16, both picture-only",
