        "body": "### ⚠️⚠️ Rows filed IN — and both are now paid\n|**Owed by**|**What was owed**|**Paid**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**`ps-mood`'s `mo-9`**|**the mood-stabilizer AGENTS** — its deck names the class on every management slide and **not one agent** — and **lithium's monitoring range**|✅ **`ph-8`**: three groups with fifteen agents, and **`0.6-1.2 mEq/L`**|\n|**`ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-10`**|the instruction to **POINT, not repeat**, for antipsychotic classes, mechanism and adverse effects|✅ **`ph-7`** points at **`sm-6`/`sm-7`** and repeats none of it — and adds the deck's own **twelve-agent classification table**, of which **eleven agents appear nowhere in book ch.7**|\n\n- **✅ The ch.11 dead heading is RESOLVED:** book ch.11 deferred *classes, mechanism of action & adverse effect* to the schizophrenia lecture; **that chapter has been read and written**, and this one points at it. **The debt that blocked `ps-pharm` for five days is closed.**\n- **⚠️ No row is filed OUT of this chapter.**\n\n### ⚠️ Two illegible items — recorded exhaustively, NEITHER inferred\n|**What**|**Why it cannot be read**|\n|---|---|\n|**The 4th AFFECTIVE symptom** of SSRI discontinuation (`ph-5`)|the lecturer's screenshot was taken with a **Google Translate floating button on screen**; the white button is **baked into the raster** over the line. Only **`…ess`** survives at 600 dpi|\n|**At least one further ROW of the antipsychotic classification table** (`ph-7`)|the pasted screenshot is **cropped through the line**. Letter-tops survive across **all four columns**, proving a row is there and **permitting not one word of it**|\n\n- **⚠️ Both are marked `[illegible]` — in the cache with the reason, and neither was completed from knowledge.** **That is the cache's contract**; this chapter may fill from outside and tag it, but **must never present the fill as the deck's.**\n\n### ⚠️ Four slides that promise and never deliver\n- **Slide 20's title ends — in an EMPTY PAIR OF PARENTHESES** — `Atypical antipsychotics()` — never filled.\n- **Slide 15** is a **photograph of a pregnancy test** with **no drug, no trimester rule, no recommendation**. **Slide 16** is **two uncaptioned images** whose intent is **unrecoverable** (`ph-6`).\n- **Slides 2, 3 and 31 are picture-only.** ⚠️ **This deck's diagnosis, from `theory-plan.md`, is THE PICTURE DECK** — **19 of 31 pages carry ZERO embedded fonts**, seven more carry **≤25 extractable characters**, and **only SIX slides carry real body text**. The transcription can still claim full coverage **because the bitmaps are screenshots of TEXT, not diagrams standing in for it.**\n- **⚠️⚠️ One line is INVISIBLE ON SCREEN:** and present in the text layer — slide 22's `• Indications:`, **covered by the MOOD STABILIZERS banner stacked on top of it**. **On a picture deck, read the text layer AND the pixels — neither alone is complete.**\n\n### What NEITHER source contains\n- **⚠️ NO DOSE — for any of the ~40 agents named here**, bar lithium's therapeutic range. **Every dose in this chapter is supplied and tagged** (`ph-1`).\n- **⚠️ NO DRUG INTERACTIONS ANYWHERE.** Serotonin syndrome is given a symptom list **with no precipitant pair named** (`ph-5`).\n- **⚠️ No MAOI adverse-effect block — in EITHER source**, nor in book ch.7 — supplied in `ph-4`.\n- **No lithium TOXIC threshold**, only the therapeutic range (`ph-8`); **no antipsychotic dose or monitoring** — `sm-3` records that ch.7 never asks for a white count on clozapine either.\n- **No benzodiazepine taper: no withdrawal or taper schedule is printed** — only the one-month ceiling.\n- **⚠️ No ECT and no TMS.** The deck's opening slide **pictures both** and the lecture never returns to them — **`ps-devices`** is their chapter, book Psychiatry ch.12 printed 265-270, **NOT READ**. **Psychotherapy is `ps-therapy`'s**, book ch.13.\n- **⚠️ A DIVERGENCE THAT IS NOT RESOLVED HERE:** the deck and book ch.7 **disagree about which dopamine pathway carries which symptom** (`ph-7`). **Both are recorded in both chapters; neither is corrected.**\n\nSrc: L17, all 31 slides, read end to end — the extraction diagnosis, the blank/title-only/picture-only inventory and both illegible items are the cache's own exhaustive lists; neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Psychiatry ch.11 printed pp. 261-264, read end to end. The register rows are audited against `ps-mood`'s `mo-9` and `ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-10`; the deck audit is recorded in content\\neuro\\theory-plan.md",
