        "h": "Register — the split, and the pain taxonomy that is verifiably absent",
        "body": "### ⚠️ The split, forecast before writing\n- **Why:** book Neurology ch.16 is **6,322 body words over SIXTEEN printed pages** (157-172) — **the longest book chapter this module has drawn on** — and `L11` adds **1,742**. **8,064 source words** forecast well past **20 pp** against the **≤13 hard shape**.\n- **The seam is the BOOK'S OWN — and it is regional:** printed **157-165 is low back and sciatica**, printed **166-172 is neck and brachialgia**. ⚠️ **And the cervical end-matter is cervical throughout** — the specific tests, `Investigations for neck pain` and `Treatment of Neck Pain` are all named for the neck — **so nothing general had to be divided.** That is what made this seam cheap.\n- **⚠️ The DECK interleaves — and the book does not.** `L11` runs **back pain → neck → low back**, so each half draws **two non-contiguous deck blocks**. **Allowed because nothing is reordered WITHIN a chapter** — the ophthalmology rule rejects a seam that would reorder an **already-written** chapter, and both halves were written fresh. **Recorded so the choice is visible.**\n- **Neither half has a question**, so nothing moved; **`SCHEDULE` is untouched.**\n\n### ⚠️ Register (§14.5) — filed OUT to `nr-neckpain`\n|**Deferred**|**Where**|\n|---|---|\n|**Neck pain and brachialgia**, and its epidemiology|printed 166 + deck|\n|**Cervical spondylosis**, **cervical disc prolapse**, **ulnar entrapment**|printed 166-167|\n|**Non-neurological systemic causes**, incl. **fibromyalgia**|printed 168|\n|**Localizing features of CERVICAL root lesions**|printed 169|\n|**The twelve SPECIFIC TESTS** — Adson's, Lhermitte's, Hoffmann's and the rest|printed 170-171|\n|**Investigations for neck pain** and **Treatment of Neck Pain**|printed 171-172|\n\n- **No row is filed IN to this chapter**, and none was owed.\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ THE PAIN TAXONOMY IS VERIFIABLY ABSENT — and one question depends on it\n- **`npqb-nr-125`** — *Migraine is best classified as which of the following?*, printed key **`Nociceptive`** — is a **`nr-headache`** question that **book Neurology ch.9 could not answer**. **Chapter 16 was read for it**, because the contents page labels its QR videos *Pain and pain management*.\n- **⚠️ IT IS NOT HERE EITHER.** The words **nociceptive**, **neuropathic**, **psychogenic**, **somatic**, **visceral** and **referred pain** *(as a taxonomy term)* **appear on none of the sixteen pages.** There is **no types-of-pain heading, no pain-mechanism table, no pain-pathway figure and no pain-management section.**\n- **⚠️ The QR labels describe a VIDEO — not printed matter** — nothing on these pages corresponds to them. **This is a VERIFIED ABSENCE, not an unread gap**, and it is the second chapter read for that one question.\n- **The closest it comes:** the only mechanism words are **`radicular pain`** (printed 160, of sciatica) and **`Neuralgic pain`** (printed 161, of myalgic sciatica) — **both descriptive, neither part of a classification.**\n\n### ⚠️ The title — the app was right and the book's contents page is wrong\n- **The opener:** ch.16 prints **`CLINICAL APPROACH TO CERVICAL AND LOW BACK PAIN`**, and **the running header on all fifteen interior pages prints `cervical and low back pain`.**\n- **A CONTENTS-PAGE TYPO: the contents page’s `Cranial and Low Back pain`** is contradicted by the chapter itself on all sixteen pages. **Recorded, corrected in neither place**; the chapter titles follow the chapter.\n\n### What this half does not contain\n- **⚠️ Three self-contradictions — all recorded and none reconciled:** **L5 topography** (`bp-4` against `bp-7`), **bed rest** (three statements, `bp-8`), and **MRI's standing** (scoped for the lumbar spine in `bp-5`, unscoped for the cervical in `nr-neckpain`).\n- **⚠️ Yellow flags are defined and never listed** (`bp-2`); **three of six differentials are named and never expanded**, two with no clause at all (`bp-5`).\n- **⚠️ Four thin headings:** whose whole body is one clause or one picture — `Management of acute LBP` (one clause), `Clinical Ɛxamination` for sciatica (**a picture only** — no SLR angle, no crossed or sensitised variant), `Rehabilitation` (**two words**), `Analgesics & Anti-Inflammatory Drugs` (**no drug, no dose**).\n- **No spinal stenosis as a topic**, **no spondylolisthesis beyond one mention** as a cause of foraminal stenosis, and **no vertebral fracture** despite trauma being red flag 2.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Neurology ch.16 printed pp. 157-165, read end to end, with the title and taxonomy findings verified across all sixteen pages; L11, read end to end. Word counts and the seam arithmetic were measured at the hub 2026-08-23. The cache is content\\neuro\\book\\neuro-ch16-pain.txt",
