        "h": "Ulnar entrapment",
        "body": "- **Where:** entrapment of the **ULNAR nerve** in the **CUBITAL TUNNEL**, at the **ELBOW**.\n\n|**Feature**|**As printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Symptoms**|**numbness, tingling and pain** referred to the **HYPOTHENAR EMINENCE** and the **LITTLE AND RING FINGERS**|\n|**⚠️ When**|**worse at NIGHT**, when the patient **sleeps with a FLEXED ELBOW** — and they **may interrupt sleep**|\n|**Sensory signs**|**decreased sensation over the PALMAR aspect of the ring and little finger**, and possibly over the **MEDIAL DORSAL aspect of the hand** and ulnar two fingers|\n|**⚠️ Severe cases**|**wasting and weakness of the small muscles of the hand**, leading to **CLAWING of the fourth and fifth digits**|\n|**Diagnosis**|**NERVE CONDUCTION STUDIES and EMG**|\n|**Treatment**|**avoiding prolonged elbow flexion** · **surgical decompression**|\n\n- **⚠️ The flexed elbow: both the cause and the clue.** Elbow flexion narrows the cubital tunnel, so the history — **woken at night, elbow bent** — **is the diagnosis**, and **avoiding that position is the first treatment**. *(The mechanism is supplied; the book prints the sign without it.)*\n- **⚠️⚠️ IT LOOKS LIKE C8 AND IT IS NOT.** Both give little-finger symptoms. **The discriminators:** an ulnar lesion spares the **medial FOREARM** — that is T1 and the medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve, above the elbow — while **C8 in `np-3` covers the medial hand AND forearm**; and an ulnar lesion gives **no neck pain and no restricted neck movement**. *(The forearm discriminator is supplied; the book prints both territories and never contrasts them.)*\n- **⚠️ This is the only entry — in the chapter that is not a spine problem**, which is why it carries its own diagnosis and its own treatment rather than sharing `np-7`'s.\n\nSrc: neuropsychiatry.pdf (ASM MINDS) Neurology ch.16 printed pp. 167-168 — `3. Ulnar Ɛntrapment` in full, with the ulnar-territory and cubital-tunnel figures. Two readings are supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4 and are marked where they occur",
