        "id": "em-5",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Managing the suicidal patient",
        "body": "### 1. Secure the environment — a checklist, not a principle\n- **SEARCH the patient thoroughly** for **toxic agents — alcohol, drugs, or hidden pills.**\n- **REMOVE:** **sharp instruments** · **glass** · **belts, straps and shoelaces** · **clothing that can be used as a ligature.**\n- **Trays: NEVER leave a MEDICATION TRAY within the patient’s reach.**\n- **NO LOCKING DOORS FROM THE INSIDE** — **especially bathrooms.**\n\n### 2. Monitor — the golden rule\n- **⚠️⚠️ NEVER LEAVE THE PATIENT ALONE.** **Line-of-sight monitoring, INCLUDING IN THE BATHROOM**; **someone accompanies them there.**\n- **The first instruction: TAKE ALL SUICIDAL THREATS OR ATTEMPTS SERIOUSLY** — `L15` prints this as the first monitoring instruction, and it is myth 1 of `em-4` turned into an order.\n\n### 3. The therapeutic presence\n- **SPEND MOST OF THE TIME WITH THE PATIENT.** **Encourage them to VENTILATE their emotions**, and **to talk about their suicidal plans and methods** — ⚠️ **asking about the plan is part of the treatment, not a risk of suggesting it.**\n- **ENHANCE SELF-ESTEEM by focusing — on their STRENGTHS**, which `L16` calls **focusing heavily on personal psychological strengths**.\n\n### 4. The emergency interview\n- **CALM, NON-JUDGEMENTAL and DIRECT**, to **ascertain CURRENT INTENT and LETHALITY** — the two variables `em-2` warns do not align.\n\n### 5. Definitive treatment\n|**What**|**Detail**|\n|---|---|\n|**Treat the UNDERLYING PSYCHIATRIC DISORDER**|the aetiology list of `em-3`|\n|**⚠️⚠️ ECT**|**AN EMERGENCY TREATMENT TOOL FOR SUICIDE** — `L16` calls it **the premier, RAPID-ACTING emergency tool to ABORT a severe suicidal crisis**|\n|**Counselling and guidance**|to deal with **the desire to attempt suicide**, with **ongoing life stressors**, and to **teach NEW COPING SKILLS**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ ECT, three times over:** the emergency answer for suicide here, for catatonia in `em-7`, for NMS in `em-9`. **`ps-devices` teaches the procedure itself** (`L18`).\n- **⚠️ Management is ENVIRONMENTAL — not pharmacological.** **Neither deck names a single drug for suicidality** — the pharmacology is the underlying disorder's, in `ps-pharm`. **That absence is deliberate and examinable.**\n\nSrc: L15 sl. Suicide (Deliberate Self-Harm) ×2 — Management, both slides, every bullet; L16 sl. Securing the Physical Environment · The Human Element of Prevention · Interviewing & Rapid Treatments",
