        "h": "Catatonia — the syndrome, and the mosaic of signs",
        "body": "|**Core feature**|**As printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**MOTORIC IMMOBILITY *or* EXCITEMENT**|`L16` splits them: **STUPOR** — motoric immobility and **lack of responsiveness**; **EXCITEMENT** — **PURPOSELESS, FRANTIC** motoric activity|\n|**PROFOUND NEGATIVISM**|`L16`: **MOTIVELESS RESISTANCE TO ALL INSTRUCTIONS**|\n|**ECHO PHENOMENA**|**ECHOLALIA** — mimicry of **speech**; **ECHOPRAXIA** — mimicry of **movement**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ One name, TWO OPPOSITE MOTOR STATES.** A patient frozen and a patient frantic are the same diagnosis — **that is exactly what makes it misinterpretable as depression, psychosis or non-compliance** (`em-1`, misstep 2).\n\n### The diagnostic mosaic — `L16`'s three groups\n|**Group**|**Signs**|\n|---|---|\n|**MOTORIC**|**CATALEPSY** · **WAXY FLEXIBILITY** · **spontaneous POSTURING**|\n|**BEHAVIOURAL**|**MUTISM** · **STEREOTYPY** · **MANNERISMS** · **AUTOMATIC OBEDIENCE**|\n|**AMBITENDENCY**|**caught in a physical HESITATION LOOP** — **repeatedly starting and stopping a movement**|\n\n- **⚠️ Two opposites, one syndrome: AUTOMATIC OBEDIENCE and PROFOUND NEGATIVISM** — and **ambitendency is the bridge between them**, the patient doing both within one movement. **Neither deck says so; the three signs are printed on adjacent slides.** *(Reading supplied.)*\n- **⚠️ `ps-symptom` defines echolalia — echopraxia, mutism, stereotypy and mannerisms as symptoms.** **This chapter is where they become a syndrome with a mortality.**\n\n### Primary or secondary — and the exclusion\n- **MEDICAL (secondary) catatonia:** a **DIRECT PHYSIOLOGICAL CONSEQUENCE of an underlying medical illness**, **laboratory-proven**.\n- **⚠️ EXCLUSION CRITERIA:** the diagnosis is **EXCLUDED if the symptoms are BETTER EXPLAINED BY A PRIMARY MENTAL DISORDER**, **or occur EXCLUSIVELY DURING ACUTE DELIRIUM** — which is `nr-delirium`'s territory.\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ The complications are what kill, and they are all mechanical\n|**System**|**Complication**|\n|---|---|\n|**Thromboembolic**|**prolonged immobility leads DIRECTLY to DVT and FATAL PE**|\n|**Nutritional**|**dehydration and electrolyte derangement**, from **mutism and negativism** — the patient will not drink|\n|**Pulmonary / skin**|**ASPIRATION PNEUMONIA** and **DECUBITUS ULCERS**|\n|**⚠️ MALIGNANT CATATONIA**|**HYPERTHERMIA and AUTONOMIC INSTABILITY** — read it against NMS in `em-8`|\n\n- **⚠️ The mechanism: four of the five follow from NOT MOVING and NOT SWALLOWING**, not from any psychiatric mechanism. **That is why `em-7`'s treatment is mostly nursing.**\n\nSrc: L15 sl. Catatonia — the four-part definition; L16 sl. Catatonia: Understanding the Syndrome · Secondary vs. Primary Catatonia · The Diagnostic Mosaic of Signs · Systemic & Lethal Complications. One reading supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4",
