        "h": "Catatonia — workup and treatment",
        "body": "### Laboratory examination\n- **⚠️⚠️ NO PATHOGNOMONIC LAB FINDING EXISTS — in catatonia.** Both decks print this in those words.\n- **What the labs are FOR:** **to RULE OUT an underlying medical condition** — `L16`: **to identify metabolic or organic triggers.**\n\n|**`L16`'s diagnostic toolkit**|\n|---|\n|**CBC** and **serum ELECTROLYTES**|\n|**RENAL and LIVER profiles**|\n|**CT / MRI BRAIN imaging**|\n|**EEG — for SUBCLINICAL SEIZURES**|\n\n- **⚠️ The EEG line is the one to carry:** **non-convulsive status epilepticus can present as an unresponsive, immobile patient**, and it is the reason an EEG sits in a psychiatric workup. **`nr-epilepsy` teaches the entity; this is the emergency in which you must think of it.** *(The link is supplied — `L16` prints only *EEG for subclinical seizures*.)*\n\n### Treatment — four supportive steps, then two treatments\n|**Step**|**Detail**|\n|---|---|\n|**1. HOSPITALISATION**|because **the patient cannot care for themselves**; **assisted with HYGIENE**|\n|**2. SUPPORTIVE CARE**|**maintenance of FLUID AND NUTRIENT INTAKE**, `L16` adds **via IV or NG TUBE**|\n|**3. CORRECTION**|**identify and correct the underlying MEDICAL or PHARMACOLOGICAL cause**|\n|**4. MINIMALISM**|`L16`'s own word — **remove ALL offending or NON-ESSENTIAL substances**|\n|**5. BENZODIAZEPINES — FIRST LINE**|**rapid, TEMPORARY improvement**; `L16`: **drastically improves communication and ENABLES SELF-CARE**|\n|**6. ECT**|`L15` lists it plainly; `L16` makes it **an EMERGENCY MANDATE if catatonia is LIFE-THREATENING (starvation) or has escalated to MALIGNANT CATATONIA**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Benzodiazepines are FIRST LINE here:** and **a DRUG OF ABUSE in `ps-sud`**, **capped at one month in `ps-pharm`’s `ph-9`**. **The same molecule, three chapters, three verdicts** — and this is the one where it is unambiguously right.\n- **⚠️ Note what is NOT given: ANTIPSYCHOTICS.** Neither deck offers one for catatonia, and **`em-1`'s third misstep is escalating antipsychotics in exactly this patient.** **Clara received haloperidol and developed NMS within 24 hours** — the case is the warning. *(The decks do not print a contraindication; the inference is mine and is drawn from their own case.)*\n- **⚠️ Steps 1-4: nursing and internal medicine.** The psychiatric contribution is **benzodiazepines and ECT** — **two items out of six.**\n\nSrc: L15 sl. Catatonia ×2 — Laboratory Examination and Treatment, all five bullets; L16 sl. Ruling Out the Medical Foundations / Diagnostic Toolkit · Stabilization & Etiological Clearance · Benzodiazepines & ECT. Two readings supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4",
