        "h": "Neuroleptic malignant syndrome — the picture, the mechanism, the labs",
        "body": "- **Definition:** a **LIFE-THREATENING NEUROLOGIC EMERGENCY ASSOCIATED WITH THE USE OF ANTIPSYCHOTIC (NEUROLEPTIC) AGENTS.** `L16` calls it **THE IATROGENIC neurologic emergency** — **the doctor causes it.**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ The tetrad\n|**Limb**|**Detail**|\n|---|---|\n|**1. MENTAL STATUS CHANGE**|`L16`: **delirium, confusion, stupor**|\n|**2. RIGIDITY**|`L16`: **LEAD-PIPE muscle rigidity**|\n|**3. FEVER**|`L16`: **HIGH fever**|\n|**4. DYSAUTONOMIA**|autonomic instability|\n\n|**Epidemiology**|**Figure**|\n|---|---|\n|**MORTALITY**|**10-20 %** — `L16` adds **if UNRECOGNISED**|\n|**INCIDENCE among patients taking antipsychotics**|**0.02-3 %**|\n|**Sex**|**MALES > FEMALES, 2:1**|\n|**⚠️ AGE**|**NOT a risk factor** — an explicit negative, and the kind of line a bank prints|\n\n### The mechanism — one blockade, two sites\n|**Site of D2 antagonism**|**What it produces**|\n|---|---|\n|**HYPOTHALAMUS**|**HYPERTHERMIA and other signs of DYSAUTONOMIA** — `L16`: **destroys central thermoregulation**|\n|**NIGROSTRIATAL**|**RIGIDITY and TREMOR** — `L16`: **severe parkinsonian extrapyramidal symptoms**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ The foundation: CENTRAL D2 RECEPTOR ANTAGONISM**, and **two of the four tetrad limbs are explained by WHERE it happens.** **`ps-pharm`'s `ph-7` and `ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-7` teach the same nigrostriatal blockade as ORDINARY extrapyramidal side effects** — **NMS is that mechanism at its extreme.**\n\n### The associated medications — three, and one is not a psychiatric drug\n|**Group**|**Agents**|\n|---|---|\n|**1. ANTIPSYCHOTICS**|**either TYPICAL or ATYPICAL**, but **MORE COMMON WITH TYPICAL**; `L16` names **HIGH-POTENCY typicals — HALOPERIDOL and FLUPHENAZINE**|\n|**2. ANTIEMETIC DRUGS**|⚠️ **METOCLOPRAMIDE and PROMETHAZINE**|\n|**3. WITHDRAWAL**|**RAPID/ABRUPT withdrawal of ANTIPARKINSONIAN drugs** — `L16`: **abrupt cessation of dopaminergic agents (LEVODOPA) in Parkinson's**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Group 2 is the trap — and group 3 is the paradox.** **Metoclopramide is prescribed for vomiting by every specialty**, and **group 3 causes NMS by REMOVING a dopamine agonist rather than by adding an antagonist** — **the same net dopamine deficit, reached from the other side.** `nr-movement` prescribes levodopa; **this is what stopping it abruptly can do.**\n\n### Laboratory findings — seven\n- **↑ WHITE BLOOD CELL COUNT** *(leukocytosis)* · **↑ CREATININE PHOSPHOKINASE (CPK)** — `L16`: **MASSIVE elevation, from muscle breakdown** · **↑ LIVER ENZYMES** · **ELECTROLYTE DISTURBANCES** · **METABOLIC ACIDOSIS** · **↑ PLASMA MYOGLOBIN** · **MYOGLOBINURIA, occasionally with RENAL FAILURE** *(`L16`: acute pigment-induced renal failure)*.\n- **⚠️ Five of the seven are one process** — **rigidity → rhabdomyolysis → CPK, myoglobin, myoglobinuria, acidosis, renal failure.** **CPK is the one to name.**\n\nSrc: L15 sl. Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome ×4 — definition and tetrad, epidemiology, mechanism and associated medications, laboratory findings; L16 sl. Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome: The Iatrogenic Neurologic Emergency · Central Dopamine Receptor Blockade · Pharmacological Culprits · Objective Biological Markers of NMS",
        "qs": []
