        "h": "What this chapter was owed, what it pays, and what it was not given",
        "body": "**§14.5 register.** Every row is a promise; an unrecorded one is a deletion.\n\n### ✅ PAID IN — two chapters filed work here, and both are settled\n|**Filed by**|**What**|**Where it landed**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**`ps-sud`'s `sd-8`**|**the WHOLE psychiatry-emergency half of `L15`, 733 w** — NMS 240, catatonia 108, suicide 385|**ALL THREE PAID.** NMS → `em-8` + `em-9` · catatonia → `em-6` + `em-7` · suicide → `em-2` to `em-5`. **Every slide of lines 205-354 is cited somewhere above.**|\n|**`ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-5`, `sm-7`, `sm-10`**|**NMS** — named twice in book ch.7 and described nowhere|**PAID IN `em-8` and `em-9`**, from the decks|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ THE SECOND ROW: recorded as a BOOK-RENDER DEBT, and it was not one.** `ps-schizmgmt` filed NMS out to **Psychiatry ch.10, image-only, unread**, on the strength of **the book's own cross-reference**, without probing the twenty-five cached decks. **`L15` teaches it in full and `L16` teaches it again** — and **`L16` adds what `L15` lacks**: lead-pipe rigidity by name, high-potency typicals by name, urinary alkalinisation, and **the whole serotonin-syndrome comparison.** Corrected there 2026-08-23.\n\n### ✅ PAID OUT — a gap this chapter closes for another\n- **`ps-pharm`'s `ph-5` records — that NEITHER of its sources names a serotonin-syndrome PRECIPITANT, an ANTIDOTE, or the MECHANISM.** **`em-10` supplies all three from `L16`** — **5-HT1A/5-HT2A**, **SSRIs+MAOIs / tramadol / fentanyl / dextromethorphan**, **CYPROHEPTADINE**, and the **Hunter criteria**. ⚠️ **`cyproheptadine` returns exactly ONE hit across all 25 decks, and it is `L16`.**\n\n### Filed out, and not written here\n|**What**|**Where it goes**|\n|---|---|\n|**ECT — the PROCEDURE**|Named **three times** here (`em-5` suicide, `em-7` catatonia, `em-9` NMS) and **described nowhere**. → **`ps-devices`**, whose deck `L18` teaches the technique, the mechanism, the stigma and the cognitive effects. **This chapter gives the INDICATIONS only** — and it holds **three of the module's emergency ones.**|\n|**Counselling, coping skills, ventilation**|`em-5` names them as management and **describes none.** → **`ps-therapy`** (`L19`).|\n|**Delirium**|`em-6`'s exclusion criterion turns on it. → **`nr-delirium`** (`L13`).|\n|**Wilson disease · Wernicke encephalopathy**|Here they are **PSYCHIATRIC PRESENTATIONS**; the diseases are **`nr-movement`'s** (`L3`) and **`ps-geri`/`nr-delirium`'s** (`L13`). ⚠️ **Wilson is in exactly two decks, `L3` and `L16`.**|\n|**Encephalitis as an infection**|`em-10`'s anti-NMDA and limbic encephalitis are **immune, not infective**. The infective ones are **`nr-cns`'s** (`L9`).|\n|**Antipsychotic pharmacology**|`em-8`'s culprits are agents, not a class table. → **`ps-pharm`'s `ph-7`** and **`ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-6`/`sm-7`**, which already hold the twelve-agent table and the D2 side-effect account. **Pointing, not repeating.**|\n\n### What the sources do not contain\n- **⚠️⚠️ NOT ONE DOSE, ANYWHERE.** A sweep for `mg` over **all 46 slides of `L16` returns ZERO**, and `L15`'s emergency half prints none either. **Benzodiazepine, dantrolene, bromocriptine, amantadine and cyproheptadine are all named without a number.** ⚠️ **Not supplied** — an emergency dose given from memory is the one place this project's fill-and-tag rule should not be used, and **`CLAUDE.md` §5 forbids writing a number from memory outright.**\n- **⚠️ Book Psychiatry ch.10 *Emergency — psychiatry medicine*, printed 256-260 — FIVE PAGES, UNREAD.** **Image-only**; a render needs a subagent and none was available. **Recorded, not guessed.** The book map calls **suicide risk and management its spine**, which the two decks cover densely — but **whether it prints doses, or an agitation/restraint protocol, is unknown.**\n- **Nothing on containment: no RESTRAINT or SEDATION protocol is printed.** `L16` warns twice about **chemical containment** and **escalating antipsychotic doses too rapidly**, and **never states what to do instead.** **Recorded as an absence, not filled.**\n- **No FOLLOW-UP or discharge criterion** for the suicidal patient in either deck.\n- **Zero questions.** No bank in the corpus prints an emergency-psychiatry question, so **there was no backwards calibration** — the same condition as `ps-sud`.\n\nSrc: register — `L15` line counts and the `mg` sweep of `L16` measured 2026-08-23; `content\\neuro\\book-map.md` row *Emergency Psychiatry → Psych 10, 256-260*; the cross-deck probes (`cyproheptadine`, `Wilson`, `serotonin syndrome`, `encephalitis`) run over all 25 cached neuro/psych lecture files",
