        "w": "must",
        "h": "Why devices at all — circuits, not chemistry",
        "body": "### The argument the lecture opens with\n|**The old model**|**The new one**|\n|---|---|\n|for decades clinical psychiatry relied heavily on the **CHEMICAL IMBALANCE MODEL** — **modulating DIFFUSE neurotransmitter systems GLOBALLY, via ORAL pharmacology**|modern psychiatry increasingly views psychiatric disorders as **conditions of DYSFUNCTION WITHIN SPECIFIC NEURAL CIRCUITS** — **DYSCONNECTIVITY**|\n|**Effective**, but it **LACKS ANATOMICAL PRECISION** — hence **SYSTEMIC SIDE EFFECTS and TREATMENT RESISTANCE**|**if the pathology is LOCALISED WITHIN A CIRCUIT, the intervention should ideally TARGET THAT CIRCUIT DIRECTLY**|\n\n- **⚠️ That is the whole rationale — and every device below is an instance of it.** Devices **change how neurons fire**, delivering results **for patients with SEVERE TREATMENT-RESISTANT conditions** — which is the population, and it is worth reading against `ps-pharm`, where **treatment resistance is what the drug chapter runs out of answers for.**\n\n### The four modalities of psychiatric treatment\n- The deck's opening figure places **DEVICES** alongside **DRUGS**, **PSYCHOTHERAPY** and **SURGERY** as the four arms of **PSYCHIATRIC TREATMENTS**. **`ps-pharm` is the first, `ps-therapy` the second; this chapter is the fourth.** **The deck names SURGERY and never returns to it** — **DBS in `dv-8` is neurosurgery, but the deck files it under devices, not under that arm.**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ And the warning, printed in the same breath\n- **The market: the hype around *BRAIN-HACKING*** has created a **MASSIVE MARKET FOR UNPROVEN GADGETS AND WELLNESS BANDS.**\n- **And the charge: many consumer devices LACK REAL SCIENTIFIC BACKING**, **EXPLOITING VULNERABLE PATIENTS** by acting as **EXPENSIVE PLACEBOS**, **DRIVEN BY BUSINESS RATHER THAN MEDICINE.**\n- **⚠️ This is not an aside — it is a running thread.** The lecture returns to it **twice more**, each time flagged where it occurs. **The deck is as interested in what is oversold as in what works.**\n\nSrc: L18 sl. Devices In Psychiatry (the four-arm figure) · the two untitled framing slides — chemical imbalance vs dysconnectivity, and the brain-hacking market",
