        "body": "|**INVASIVE**|**NON-INVASIVE**|\n|---|---|\n|**ECT** — electroconvulsive therapy, **also written BST, Brain Synchronization Therapy** (`dv-5`)|**TMS / rTMS** — transcranial magnetic stimulation|\n|**DBS** — deep brain stimulation|**tDCS** — transcranial direct current stimulation|\n|**VNS** — vagus nerve stimulation|**EEG NEUROFEEDBACK systems**|\n| |**OTHER AI RECENT DEVICES**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ ECT IS FILED AS INVASIVE — AND IT INVOLVES NO INCISION.** The deck's line is **invasive**, and what makes it so is **general anaesthesia and an induced generalised seizure**, not surgery — whereas **DBS and VNS are invasive in the ordinary surgical sense** (`dv-8`). **Three devices, one label, two different meanings** — a place a bank question can be built. *(The distinction is drawn out here; the deck prints only the two lists.)*\n\nSrc: L18 sl. Invasive Devices / Non-invasive Devices, both lists verbatim. One reading supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4",
