        "h": "ECT — the numbers, and the exact procedure",
        "body": "**⚠️ A row paid: this section and the two that follow** settle what `ps-emerg`’s `em-11` and `ps-schizmgmt`’s `sm-10` both filed — each names ECT and describes it nowhere. **`dv-10` audits what arrived, item by item.**\n\n|**Fact**|**As printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Introduced**|**1938** — **one of the OLDEST treatments in modern psychiatry**|\n|**Standing**|**it remains IRREPLACEABLE in clinical practice**, despite decades of pharmacological expansion|\n|**⚠️⚠️ Efficacy**|**THE MOST EFFECTIVE ACUTE TREATMENT AVAILABLE FOR SEVERE MOOD DISORDERS**, with a **70-80 % RESPONSE RATE** — ** in patients who have FAILED MULTIPLE TRIALS OF ANTIDEPRESSANTS**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Read — that response rate against the population it is measured in.** **70-80 % is not in a fresh cohort** — it is in patients **who have already failed multiple drugs**, which is what makes the figure remarkable and what makes *irreplaceable* a defensible word. **It is the single most quotable number in the chapter.**\n\n### The procedure\n|**Step**|**Detail**|\n|---|---|\n|**Anaesthesia**|performed under **GENERAL ANAESTHESIA** with a **MUSCLE RELAXANT — SUCCINYLCHOLINE** — **to prevent physical movement**|\n|**The stimulus**|a **BRIEF, CONTROLLED ELECTRICAL STIMULUS**, applied **TRANSCRANIALLY**, **UNILATERAL or BILATERAL**|\n|**The endpoint**|to **INDUCE A GENERALISED THERAPEUTIC SEIZURE lasting 20-60 SECONDS**|\n|**Recovery**|**the patient WAKES WITHIN MINUTES, COMPLETELY UNAWARE OF THE SEIZURE**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ The muscle relaxant answers the stigma** — see `dv-5`. **The seizure is electrical and generalised; the body does not convulse**, because succinylcholine has paralysed it. **The public image of ECT is an image of the pre-1950s procedure.**\n- **⚠️ The deck’s own phrase: *therapeutic seizure*.** The target is **20-60 seconds**, and **a seizure is the INTENDED endpoint here** — the opposite of everything `nr-epilepsy` is about. **Same event, opposite sign.**\n\nSrc: L18 sl. ECT: The Oldest, Most Effective Tool in the Shed · ECT: The exact procedure, both slides in full",
