        "h": "ECT — five indications, and a mechanism that is not fully understood",
        "body": "|**Indication**|**As printed, and where it is taught**|\n|---|---|\n|**1. TREATMENT-RESISTANT DEPRESSION (TRD)**|**when multiple drugs fail** — `ps-mood`, `ps-pharm`|\n|**2. SEVERE CATATONIA**|**OFTEN LIFE-SAVING; HIGHLY RESPONSIVE TO ECT** — `ps-emerg`'s `em-7`, where it is an **emergency mandate** if catatonia is life-threatening or malignant|\n|**3. ACUTE SUICIDALITY**|**when IMMEDIATE BIOLOGICAL INTERVENTION IS REQUIRED TO SAVE A LIFE** — `em-5`, which calls it **the premier rapid-acting tool to ABORT a suicidal crisis**|\n|**4. SEVERE MANIA OR PSYCHOSIS**|**in TREATMENT-RESISTANT BIPOLAR DISORDER or SCHIZOPHRENIA** — `ps-mood`, `ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-8`|\n|**5. ⚠️ LESS COMMON USES**|**PARKINSONIAN CRISIS** · **STATUS EPILEPTICUS** — the deck writes the second with two exclamation marks of its own|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Indication 5 is the strangest line — in the module and the deck knows it.** **ECT is used to treat STATUS EPILEPTICUS** — an induced seizure given for an unremitting one. **`nr-epilepsy` does not mention it.** *(The deck offers no explanation, and none is supplied here.)*\n- **⚠️ Three of the five are EMERGENCIES** — catatonia, suicidality, parkinsonian crisis — and **`ps-emerg` reaches for ECT in all three of its topics.** **Add NMS**, where `em-9` lists ECT as step 9 of the treatment, and **ECT is the common terminal answer across the whole emergency chapter.**\n\n### Mechanism — **NOT FULLY UNDERSTOOD**, in the deck's own capitals\n|**Proposed mechanism**|**What is claimed**|\n|---|---|\n|**NEUROTRANSMITTER RESET**|induces a **MASSIVE, SIMULTANEOUS RELEASE AND UPREGULATION** of **SEROTONIN, DOPAMINE and NOREPINEPHRINE RECEPTORS**|\n|**NEUROPLASTICITY SURGE**|strongly stimulates the release of **BDNF — BRAIN-DERIVED NEUROTROPHIC FACTOR**, **inducing NEUROGENESIS (new neuron growth) IN THE HIPPOCAMPUS**|\n|**NETWORK FUNCTIONAL CONNECTIVITY**|**CALMS THE HYPERACTIVE functional connectivity** seen in the **DEFAULT MODE NETWORK (DMN)** of severely depressed brains|\n\n- **⚠️ Three mechanisms at three scales** — **molecular** (receptors), **cellular** (neurogenesis), **network** (the DMN) — and **the deck commits to none of them.** *NOT FULLY UNDERSTOOD* is printed in capitals on the slide, and **that honesty is itself examinable: the most effective acute treatment in psychiatry has no agreed mechanism.**\n- **⚠️ The same three monoamines as `ps-pharm`** — serotonin, dopamine, noradrenaline. **The claim here is UPREGULATION of receptors, not reuptake inhibition**; a different action on the same system, and **the DMN and BDNF appear nowhere else in the module.**\n\nSrc: L18 sl. ECT: when used and how it works ? — both columns, all five indications and all three mechanisms as printed",
