        "id": "dv-5",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "ECT — the stigma, the proposed rename, and the one real drawback",
        "body": "### Perception\n- **MEDIA DEPICTIONS** — the deck names ***One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest*** — **historically associate ECT with PUNISHMENT AND PAIN.**\n- **⚠️ The error in it: that depiction COMPLETELY IGNORES MODERN ANAESTHESIA**, and the result is **WIDESPREAD PUBLIC AND PATIENT FEAR.**\n- **⚠️⚠️ A NEW NAME IS PROPOSED: BRAIN SYNCHRONISING THERAPY (BST)**, to overcome the stigma. **That is why the invasive list in `dv-2` prints *ECT / BST*** — **the two are the same treatment**, and a bank could reasonably ask for either expansion.\n\n### Reality\n|**Claim**|**As printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Safety**|**ECT IS A HIGHLY SAFE PROCEDURE DESPITE ITS BAD REPUTATION**|\n|**⚠️ The TRUE primary clinical drawback**|**TRANSIENT COGNITIVE DISRUPTION**, and **ANTEROGRADE / RETROGRADE MEMORY GAPS AROUND THE TREATMENT PERIOD**|\n|**What reduces it**|**MODERN ULTRA-BRIEF PULSE WIDTH DELIVERY SIGNIFICANTLY MINIMISES these cognitive side effects**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Note what the drawback is NOT: it is not pain, not danger, and not brain damage.** It is **memory, it is TRANSIENT, and it is AROUND THE TREATMENT PERIOD** — and **the deck names a specific engineering answer to it, ULTRA-BRIEF PULSE WIDTH.** **The stigma and the real risk are two different things, and the examinable point is that they do not coincide.**\n- **⚠️ Both directions of amnesia are named** — **ANTEROGRADE and RETROGRADE.** `ps-symptom` defines the pair; **this is the module's cleanest iatrogenic instance of it.**\n\nSrc: L18 sl. ECT: The Controversy & Stigma (Perception vs. Reality), both halves in full",
