        "id": "dv-6",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "TMS — the physics, the target, the indications",
        "body": "### How it differs from ECT, and how it works\n|**Feature**|**As printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**Invasiveness**|**COMPLETELY NON-INVASIVE**, and **performed while the patient is FULLY AWAKE** — no anaesthesia, no seizure|\n|**The hardware**|an **ELECTROMAGNETIC COIL placed AGAINST THE SCALP**|\n|**The field**|**LOCALISED, HIGH-INTENSITY MAGNETIC PULSES, around 1.5 to 2 TESLA** — **similar to an MRI machine**|\n|**⚠️ The physics**|the magnetic fields **PASS THROUGH THE SKULL ENTIRELY UNIMPEDED**, **inducing a TARGETED FOCAL ELECTRICAL CURRENT in the underlying cortical tissue**|\n|**The effect on neurons**|to **DEPOLARISE or HYPERPOLARISE local neurons** at certain brain regions|\n|**The depression target**|the **LEFT DORSOLATERAL PREFRONTAL CORTEX (DLPFC)**, which **RESTORES FUNCTIONAL CONNECTIVITY DOWN TO DEEPER LIMBIC SYSTEMS**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Magnetic in, electrical out.** The coil is magnetic **precisely because a magnetic field crosses bone unimpeded and an electrical one does not**; the current that actually acts on neurons is **induced in the cortex.** **That conversion is the single idea behind the device**, and it is why TMS reaches only the **cortex** while `dv-8`'s DBS must be implanted to reach deeper.\n- **⚠️ 1.5-2 Tesla is the one number to carry**, and the MRI comparison is the deck's own.\n\n### The clinical landscape — five indications\n|**Indication**|**Detail, and the target where one is named**|\n|---|---|\n|**1. TREATMENT-RESISTANT MDD**|**THE PRIMARY MAINSTREAM INDICATION**; **approved for BOTH ADULTS AND ADOLESCENTS**|\n|**2. OCD**|typically **DEEP TMS (dTMS)** with a **specialised H-COIL**, targeting the **SUPPLEMENTARY MOTOR AREA (SMA)** and **ANTERIOR CINGULATE CORTEX** — `ps-ocd`|\n|**3. ANXIOUS DEPRESSION**|**comorbid anxiety symptoms within a major depressive episode** — `ps-anxiety`, `ps-mood`|\n|**4. SMOKING CESSATION**|a **targeted ADDICTION protocol**, **reducing cravings** by stimulating the **BILATERAL PREFRONTAL CORTEX and INSULA** — `ps-sud`|\n|**5. MIGRAINE WITH AURA**|**ACUTE pain management**, using **ACUTE HANDHELD SINGLE-PULSE devices** — `nr-headache`|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Every indication has its own coil — target and protocol.** **Depression: left DLPFC. OCD: an H-coil to SMA and anterior cingulate. Smoking: bilateral PFC and insula. Migraine: a handheld single-pulse device.** **TMS is not one treatment** — and **indication 4 pays a gap `ps-sud` recorded**, whose deck offers **no pharmacotherapy at all for craving beyond four substances.**\n- **⚠️ Indication 5 stands apart:** it is **the only NEUROLOGICAL one here**, and it is **acute, not preventive** — **`nr-headache` prints no device in either of its treatment lists.**\n\nSrc: L18 sl. TMS (Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation) · The Clinical Landscape of TMS, all five indications with their targets as printed",
