        "body": "**§14.5 register.** Every row is a promise; an unrecorded one is a deletion.\n\n### ✅ PAID IN — two chapters filed ECT here, and this is the audit of what arrived\n`ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-8` records ECT as **a ONE-LINE section, indications only**, and lists **six things it does not print**. **Each is checked against `L18` below, second clause and all** — because a *row filed* claim that is never measured is how five wrong rows survived in ophthalmology.\n\n|**What `sm-8` said was missing**|**State against `L18`**|\n|---|---|\n|**TECHNIQUE**|✅ **PAID** — `dv-3`, the full four-step procedure|\n|**ANAESTHESIA**|✅ **PAID** — **general anaesthesia + SUCCINYLCHOLINE**, named|\n|**ADVERSE EFFECT**|✅ **PAID** — `dv-5`, **transient cognitive disruption and anterograde/retrograde memory gaps**, and the ultra-brief-pulse answer|\n|**ELECTRODE PLACEMENT**|⚠️ **PARTIAL** — ***unilateral or bilateral*** is all `L18` prints. **No selection rule, no montage.**|\n|**COURSE LENGTH**|❌ **STILL ABSENT.** `L18` gives the seizure duration (20-60 s) and **not one word on how many treatments, or how often**|\n|**CONTRAINDICATION**|❌ **STILL ABSENT** — and see the sweep below|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ AND THE POINTER `sm-8` GAVE WAS WRONG.** It sent ECT to **book Psychiatry ch.12, printed 265-270, *not read*** — an image-only render nobody could do. **`L18` was cached the whole time.** **Four of six items are paid from a deck already on disk.** Corrected in `sm-5`/`sm-7`/`sm-10` and in MEMORY on 2026-08-23; **this row is the measurement that closes it.**\n- **`ps-emerg`'s `em-11` filed the same debt** — ECT **named three times and described nowhere.** ✅ **PAID by `dv-3` to `dv-5`.**\n\n### ⚠️ One divergence between the two sources, recorded and not resolved\n- **`ps-emerg`'s `em-9` gives ECT — as STEP 9 of the NMS treatment**, from `L15`. **`L18`'s five-item indication list does NOT include NMS** — its *less common uses* are **parkinsonian crisis** and **status epilepticus**. **Neither deck is wrong; they are different lists made for different purposes.** **Both stand as printed** (`CLAUDE.md` §4).\n\n### Filed out, and not written here\n|**What**|**Where it goes**|\n|---|---|\n|**CBT, exposure therapy, operant conditioning**|`dv-9`'s VR headsets deliver **graded exposure**, its chatbots deliver **text-based CBT**, and neurofeedback **relies on operant conditioning** — **all three are named and none is explained.** → **`ps-therapy`** (`L19`).|\n|**ADHD**|`dv-9`'s theta/beta protocol and `dv-7`'s off-label list both turn on it. → **`ps-child`** (`L14`).|\n|**The OCD circuit**|`dv-8`'s **CSTC loop** is the anatomy `ps-ocd` uses for the disorder itself. **Pointing, not repeating.**|\n|**Parkinson's · refractory epilepsy · migraine with aura · chronic neuropathic pain**|the four **NEUROLOGICAL** indications scattered across `dv-4`, `dv-6`, `dv-8`, `dv-9`. → **`nr-movement`, `nr-epilepsy`, `nr-headache`, `nr-backpain`**, none of which prints a device.|\n|**Treatment resistance**|the population **every device in this chapter is for.** → **`ps-pharm`**, `ps-mood`, `ps-schizmgmt`'s `sm-8` (clozapine).|\n\n### What the source does not contain\n- **⚠️⚠️ NOT ONE CONTRAINDICATION — FOR ANY DEVICE.** **`contraindicat` returns ZERO across all 23 slides of `L18`** — no cardiac, no raised-intracranial-pressure, no pregnancy, no pacemaker, no metal-implant caution for TMS. ⚠️ **NOT SUPPLIED**: a contraindication list written from memory would be six device-specific lists, and **`CLAUDE.md` §5 forbids writing them from memory.** **Recorded as the chapter's largest hole.**\n- **⚠️ No CONSENT or capacity discussion**, for a chapter whose flagship treatment needs general anaesthesia and carries a stigma. **`consent` returns zero in `L18`** and appears in **`L19` alone** across all 25 decks.\n- **⚠️⚠️ A SYLLABUS-LEVEL ABSENCE:** **PSYCHOSURGERY is named as one of the four arms of psychiatric treatment (`dv-1`) and taught NOWHERE.** **`psychosurgery`, `cingulotomy` and `lobotomy` return ZERO across ALL 25 CACHED DECKS.** **DBS is neurosurgery filed under devices** — and **the surgical arm itself has no lecture in this module.** **Verified at the level of the whole syllabus, not of one chapter.**\n- **⚠️ Two quantified parameters — in the whole chapter**: **TMS at 1.5-2 Tesla** and **tDCS at 1-2 mA**. **ECT’s charge, pulse width and course are not; DBS’s frequency is not; VNS’s duty cycle is not.**\n- **⚠️ No number for TMS: its remission rate is never quantified** — *relatively modest real-world remission rate* is all `dv-7` has, and it is the one place a figure would settle the cost-effectiveness argument the deck itself raises.\n- **⚠️ Book Psychiatry ch.12 *Devices — in psychiatry*, printed 265-270 — SIX PAGES, UNREAD.** **Image-only**; a render needs a subagent and none was available. **Recorded, not guessed** — it is the likeliest home for the contraindications and the course length.\n- **Zero questions.** No bank in the corpus prints a device question, so **there was no backwards calibration** — the third chapter running in this condition, after `ps-sud` and `ps-emerg`.\n\nSrc: register — the `contraindicat` / `consent` / `psychosurgery` / `cingulotomy` / `lobotomy` sweeps run over all 25 cached neuro/psych lecture files 2026-08-23; `sm-8`'s six-item list read from `content\\neuro\\theory-drafts\\ps-schizmgmt.draft.js`; `content\\neuro\\book-map.md` row *Devices in Psychiatry → Psych 12, 265-270*",
