        "h": "What psychotherapy is, and where it sits",
        "body": "### What the word covers\n- **Psychotherapy:** the general term for **treating psychological disorder and mental distress through VERBAL and PSYCHOLOGICAL techniques.**\n- **Also called:** *talk therapy*, *counselling*, *psychosocial therapy*, or simply *therapy*.\n\n### What kind of treatment it is\n- **Collaborative —** built on the **relationship between an individual and a psychologist.**\n- **Grounded in dialogue —** it provides a **supportive environment** for talking openly with someone **objective, neutral and non-judgmental.**\n- **The work is joint —** patient and therapist together **identify and change the thought and behaviour patterns** keeping the patient from feeling their best.\n\n### Who may provide it\n- **Medical and nursing:** psychiatrists · psychiatric nurses.\n- **Psychology and social work:** psychologists · licensed social workers.\n- **Family and marriage:** licensed marriage and family therapists.\n- **And the open clause:** *others with specialized training in psychotherapy* — the deck's own wording, and it does not close the list.\n\n### ⚠️ Two decks, two different lists of the treatment arms\n|**Deck**|**The arms it names**|\n|---|---|\n|**L1,2** *Psychiatric sheet*|**1) Hospitalization · 2) Psychotherapy · 3) Psychopharmacology · 4) Biological therapies**, e.g. **ECT**|\n|**L18** *Devices in Psychiatry*|**DRUGS · PSYCHOTHERAPY · DEVICES · SURGERY**|\n\n- **⚠️ The two disagree, and both are recorded.** **Psychotherapy is the only arm the two name identically.** **L1,2 folds the devices into *biological therapies*; L18 breaks them out as their own arm and adds SURGERY** — which, as `ps-devices` `dv-10` records, **is taught nowhere in the module.**\n- *Pharmacotherapy is `ps-pharm`; devices are `ps-devices`. This chapter is the arm both lists share.*\n\nSrc: L19 sl. What is Psychotherapy · Psychotherapy (incl. Who can provide psychotherapy?) — both in full. Arms table: L1,2 sl. management list · L18 four-arm figure via `ps-devices` `dv-1`",
