        "body": "### The claim\n- **Symptom relief:** **most people experience symptom relief and are BETTER ABLE TO FUNCTION IN THEIR LIVES.**\n- **⚠️ The one figure in the slide — 75 PER CENT:** *75 percent show some benefit from it.* **It is the deck's only quantified outcome, and it is a benefit rate, not a cure rate.**\n- **Mechanistic claim:** psychotherapy **improves emotions and behaviours** and is **linked with POSITIVE CHANGES IN THE BRAIN AND BODY.**\n\n### The four benefits it lists beyond symptoms\n- **Fewer sick days.**\n- **Less disability.**\n- **Fewer medical problems.**\n- **Increased work satisfaction.**\n\n- **⚠️ The chart slide cannot be read:** the second *Does Psychotherapy Work?* panel carries **six extracted words and a 1280x720 image**. **Whatever it quantifies is not recoverable without a render.** Recorded, not guessed.\n\nSrc: L19 sl. Does Psychotherapy Work? ×2 — the prose slide in full; the chart slide is an image (measured: 6 words of text, one 1280x720 image)",
