        "body": "### The nine the deck lists\n- **Stress or anxiety** caused by **work or any other situation.**\n- **Conflicts** with a **partner, family member or friend.**\n- **Major life changes —** **divorce**, **death of a loved one**, **loss of a job.**\n- **Recovery from abuse —** **physical or sexual abuse**, or **being a WITNESS to violence.**\n- **Unhealthy reactions —** learning to manage them, e.g. **aggressive behaviours.**\n- **Ongoing or serious physical illness —** e.g. **cancer** or **chronic pain.**\n- **Sleep —** getting better sleep, e.g. **insomnia.**\n- **Low self-esteem.**\n- **Low quality of life in any other way.**\n\n- **⚠️ Indexed by PROBLEM, not by diagnosis** — the only place in the module a psychiatric treatment is presented that way, and **two of the nine are not psychiatric diagnoses at all** (chronic physical illness, quality of life). *That reading is mine; the nine items are the deck's.*\n\n### Predictors of response\n- **YAVIS —** an acronym **coined to indicate that clients improve MORE in psychotherapy when they are** *young, attractive, verbal, intelligent, and successful.*\n- **⚠️ But the best predictor is not the client:** *to date, the best predictor of outcome in ANY psychotherapy is the **DEGREE OF THE THERAPEUTIC ALLIANCE**.*\n- **⚠️ One hit in the module —** `therapeutic alliance` appears **on this slide and nowhere else across the 25 decks**, and the deck makes it the single strongest predictor it prints.\n\nSrc: L19 sl. It can help with: — all nine verbatim · Predictors of response to psychotherapy, both statements verbatim",
