        "h": "Ethics and professional practice — six headings, no text",
        "body": "### What the slide prints\n- **Six headings, no text —** not one sentence under any of them. The deck's **last teaching slide** before *THANK YOU!* prints them bare: **Best interests of clients · Professionalism · Communication and consent · Records and confidentiality · Professional knowledge, skills and experience · Social responsibility.**\n\n### What each heading covers\n*Glosses supplied so the headings are usable; **none of this is taken from the course material**, and nothing here is a rule, a threshold or a legal standard.*\n\n|**Heading**|**What it means in practice**|\n|---|---|\n|**Best interests of clients**|the client's welfare governs the treatment plan, **above the therapist's convenience, curiosity or theoretical preference**|\n|**Professionalism**|**boundaries** — no dual relationships, no exploitation of the dependency therapy creates|\n|**Communication and consent**|the client is told **what the therapy involves and what its alternatives are**, and **agrees to it**|\n|**Records and confidentiality**|**what is said stays in the room and what is written stays secured**, with the recognised exception of **risk to the client or to others**|\n|**Professional knowledge, skills and experience**|**practise within your competence** and keep it current|\n|**Social responsibility**|the profession answers to **the public**, not only to its clients|\n\n### ⚠️ Two words that appear only here\n- **`consent` —** returns **exactly one hit across all 25 cached decks**, this slide. **No consent procedure is taught anywhere in the module** — not for ECT, not for admission, not for restraint. `ps-devices` records the same absence from the device side.\n- **`confidential` —** **two hits**: here, and **L6's myth #5**, where *therapy is CONFIDENTIAL and OBJECTIVE* is the answer to *only people without friends need therapists* (`ps-psychoed`).\n\nSrc: L19 sl. Ethics and Professional practice — all six headings verbatim, and the slide carries nothing else. Glosses supplied per `CLAUDE.md` §4. Word sweeps run over all 25 cached decks",
