        "h": "The register — 21 questions audited, and what is deliberately elsewhere",
        "body": "### All 21 questions checked against the sources BEFORE writing\n*The ophthalmology rule: **a Decks column is an assignment, not coverage.** **All 21 are answerable**, and the table says from where. ⚠️ **This register covers the PAIR** — the chapter was written whole, printed at 14 pages and split; **seven questions sit in `nr-intro`, fourteen here**, moved by their theory `qs` links and not by title.*\n\n|**Asks**|**Answered in**|\n|---|---|\n|deep-sensation tracts · dorsal-column lesion · thalamic relay and its exception|`nr-intro` `in-5` — book **p.31**, **p.36**|\n|C4 compression and the triceps · hyperreflexia causes · absent abdominal · biceps and brachioradialis roots · grade 3 · plantar|`nx-2` — book **p.21**, **p.22**|\n|power grade 2 · power grade 3 · spasticity against rigidity|`nx-1` — book **p.18**, **p.19**|\n|Broca's aphasia · motor cortex · somatosensory cortex|`nr-intro` `in-6` — book **p.11**, **pp.28-29**|\n|homonymous hemianopia · inferior quadrantanopia|`nr-intro` `in-7` — book **p.12**|\n|lateral-column lesion · hemisection · segmental sensory loss|`nx-3` — book **p.23**, **p.38**|\n\n- **⚠️ Twelve of the 21 carry a TAG:** an **OUTSIDE-KNOWLEDGE** tag in their explanations, written when no source covered them. **Those tags were CORRECT** — they say no cached **deck** covers the fact, and a sweep re-run 2026-08-23 confirms it: **`optic radiation`, `Broca`, `abdominal reflex`, `brachioradialis` and reflex grading return ZERO across all 25 decks.** **The book now supplies every one.** ⚠️ **Re-grounding those twelve explanations is a SCOPED FOLLOW-ON JOB recorded in plan §5 and NOT done here** — the banks are paused, and it is not to be swept silently into a theory session.\n\n### What the pair does not write\n- **The deferrals are `nr-intro`'s:** recorded in its `in-8` — **UMN/LMN manifestations → `nr-lmn` `lm-1`** (L1's slides, counted there) · **hemiplegia, L1's whole back half → `nr-hemi`** (checked against `hem-1` to `hem-6`, not assumed) · **ataxia → `hem-14`/`hem-15`** · **the cranial nerves → `nr-cranial`** · **spinal shock → `hem-9`.**\n\n### ⚠️ Verified absences — looked for, not found, and NOT filled\n- **NO NAMED BRAINSTEM SYNDROME, anywhere** — **Weber, Millard-Gubler and Wallenberg appear nowhere in the book.** Printed p.31 lists the cranial nerve nuclei by level, and printed p.39 sets **left midbrain with the CN III nucleus** and **left pons with the CN VII nucleus** as **exercises**. *The crossed rule the decks never print is `nr-hemi` `hem-5`.*\n- **HORNER'S SYNDROME EXISTS ONLY AS A FIGURE** (printed p.27 — hemisection at T1, anhidrosis, miosis, ptosis, same side as the lesion). **No body text anywhere.**\n- **`TOPMAGII` — four functions, never expanded:** the book prints it as a mnemonic, lists only four functions under it, and **never expands the acronym.**\n- **The GCS is named and never scored** — printed p.10 defers it with *See coma lecture* and prints three external URLs. **Not visited, not supplied.**\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ Source faults carried into this chapter, every one recorded and none corrected\n- **Eight, each recorded where it occurs:** the **power grade 3 bullet** (`nx-1`) · the **dorsal-column decussation, pons against medulla** (`nr-intro` `in-5`) · **quadriplegia against tetraplegia**, and the **Brown-Séquard accent** (`nx-3`) · **`Boca's aphasia`** (`nr-intro` `in-6`) · **four pathological reflexes named with no method** (`nx-2`) · **ten clinical quizzes the book NEVER KEYS** and **ch.1's four unsolved vignettes** (`nr-intro` `in-1`).\n- **⚠️ Much of ch.3 is FIGURE-ONLY:** the **anterior corticospinal tract**, **fasciculations**, **muscle atrophy**, **Babinski by name**, **Broca and Wernicke**, the **cortical arterial territories** and the **components of the corpus striatum** are each named in a figure and **in no sentence.** The caches flag every one in place.\n\nSrc: register. Question audit run against `questions.neuro.js` and the three book caches 2026-08-23. Deck sweeps for `optic radiation`, `Broca`, `abdominal reflex`, `brachioradialis` and reflex grading run over all 25 cached decks. `nr-hemi` and `nr-lmn` drafts read from disk before deferring, not assumed",
