        "id": "ci-6",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Acute bacterial meningitis — CSF, treatment and prevention",
        "body": "### CSF analysis — six lines, with the numbers\n|**Line**|**Acute bacterial meningitis**|\n|---|---|\n|**Pressure**|**INCREASED**|\n|**Cells**|**INCREASED, usually 1,000–10,000/dl, mainly NEUTROPHILS**|\n|**Protein**|**INCREASED, usually ABOVE 45 mg/dl (100–500 mg/dl)**|\n|**Sugar**|**DECREASED — LESS THAN 40 mg/dl, or < 40 % OF BLOOD SUGAR**|\n|**Stain**|**GRAM STAINING**|\n|**Culture**|**CULTURE AND SENSITIVITY TEST**|\n\n- *⚠️ The deck writes the cell count as `/dl`, and it is transcribed as printed. A CSF cell count is conventionally per microlitre; the unit is noted, not corrected.*\n\n### Radiological investigations\n- **CT and MRI brain** — **in case of LATERALIZATION or SUSPICIOUS INCREASE IN INTRACRANIAL PRESSURE.** *(The pre-tap imaging rule and the LP contraindications are in `ci-3`.)*\n\n### Treatment — general principles\n- **HOSPITALIZATION.**\n- **⚠️ MINIMUM DURATION OF ANTIBIOTIC THERAPY — BOTH conditions, not either:** **AT LEAST 10 DAYS FROM THE START OF TREATMENT**, **AND AT LEAST 7 DAYS AFTER THE PATIENT BECOMES AFEBRILE.**\n\n### Recommended empiric antibiotics\n- **VANCOMYCIN + CEFTRIAXONE**, by **anti-meningitic dose.**\n- **CORTICOSTEROIDS — DEXAMETHASONE INJECTION: DECREASES MORTALITY AND SEQUELAE.**\n- **The rule:** **empirical treatment is given UNTIL THE RESULTS OF CSF CULTURE AND SENSITIVITY ARE AVAILABLE**, and **then the SPECIFIC antibiotic is given.**\n- **⚠️ The only quantification:** the slide writes **\"by anti-meningitic dose\"** and **no milligram figure** for vancomycin, for ceftriaxone or for the dexamethasone. **Deliberately NOT supplied** — an antibiotic dose written from memory is exactly what this project's citation rule forbids.\n\n### Prevention\n- **CHEMOPROPHYLAXIS —** **FOR CONTACTS of the patient**, and here the deck *does* print doses:\n  - **Adults — CIPROFLOXACIN 500 mg, SINGLE DOSE.**\n  - **Children — EITHER a SINGLE DOSE OF CEFTRIAXONE IM, or 4 ORAL DOSES OF RIFAMPIN.**\n- **VACCINATION — POLYSACCHARIDE POLYVALENT VACCINE against MENINGOCOCCAL MENINGITIS.**\n- **⚠️ The gap:** **the deck vaccinates against the MENINGOCOCCUS ONLY.** **No pneumococcal and no H. influenzae type b vaccine appears anywhere in it** — although **both organisms sit in its own 80 % triad** (`ci-4`).\n\nSrc: L9 sl. Acute Bacterial Meningitis: CSF ANALYSIS · Radiological investigations / Treatment · Recommended Empiric Antibiotics · Prevention — all in full",
