        "body": "### §14.5 register — deferred OUT of this chapter\n*Every row below was verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js read from disk, section by section — not against a promise.*\n\n|**Fact, and where it arises here**|**Owed to**|**Written?**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**TODD'S PARALYSIS** — a mechanism of focal signs, `ci-5`|`nr-epilepsy` · `nr-hemi`|✅ **already written** — `ep-1` (the post-ictal state) and `ep-3` (the collapse differential); `hem-2` carries it as a cause of transient hemiplegia|\n|**STATUS EPILEPTICUS** — Case 2, `ci-10`|`nr-epilepsy`|✅ **already written** — `ep-10`, definition and the emergency protocol|\n|**PAPILLOEDEMA** — the imaging trigger, `ci-3`|`nr-cranial`|✅ **already written** — `cn-3`, on the fundoscopy row|\n|**HYDROCEPHALUS** and its drainage — `ci-5`, `ci-7`|`nr-stroke`|✅ **already written** — `str-10`, among the SAH complications|\n|**AUTOIMMUNE ENCEPHALITIS** — the non-infective encephalitis L9 omits, `ci-9`|`nr-epilepsy` · `ps-emerg`|✅ **already written** — `ep-6` (anti-NMDAR, LGI1) and `em-1` (the case mimicking psychosis)|\n|**SPINAL / VERTEBRAL TB (POTT'S DISEASE)** — TB of the nervous system outside the meninges|`nr-para` · `nr-neckpain`|✅ **already written** — L11 and L12 carry it, and **L9 never mentions it**|\n\n### Received INTO this chapter\n- **`nr-cranial` `cn-5`** — **tuberculous meningitis as a cause of a sixth-nerve palsy**, from L8. Used in `ci-7` to corroborate L9's own cranial-nerve claim from a second deck.\n\n### ⚠️ Verified absences — probed across all 25 cached decks, not assumed\n|**What**|**What the probe returned**|\n|---|---|\n|**CRYPTOCOCCAL MENINGITIS**|`cryptococc` returns **ONE hit in 25 decks — L9's own taxonomy slide.** **Named as the fungal class and never taught.** **Nothing is supplied:** a whole clinical entity written from memory is not a gap-fill|\n|**VIRAL MENINGITIS as an entity**|`viral meningitis` returns **one hit — the same taxonomy slide.** **No slide of its own**; the aseptic criteria (`ci-8`) are the nearest the lecture comes|\n|**SUBDURAL EMPYEMA**|**named in TWO decks — L9 and L1's coma list — and DEFINED IN NEITHER.** One line supplied and tagged in `ci-5`|\n|**BRAIN ABSCESS**|**named in THREE decks — L9, L1, L12 — and expanded in none**|\n|**ANY DOSE for the empirical antibiotics**|the slide writes **\"by anti meningitic dose\"** and **no milligram figure** for vancomycin, ceftriaxone or dexamethasone. **NOT supplied.** The **prophylaxis** doses that ARE printed are transcribed in `ci-6`, and the **acyclovir** dose in `ci-9`|\n|**PNEUMOCOCCAL and Hib VACCINATION**|the prevention slide vaccinates against **the meningococcus only** — although **both organisms are in its own 80 % triad**|\n|**NEUROSYPHILIS · POLIO · NEUROCYSTICERCOSIS · RABIES · TETANUS**|**NOT ONE of them appears in L9** — the lecture's five entities are the whole of its scope. ⚠️ **Three of the five DO exist elsewhere in the module, as LIST ITEMS ONLY:** `syphilis` in **L12** and **L13** (`nr-para`; and the L13 pair `ps-geri`/`nr-delirium`, **not yet written**) · `polio` in **L12, L5, L6** (`nr-para`, `nr-lmn`, `nr-nerve`) · `neurocysticercosis` **once**, in **L4**'s acute-symptomatic-seizure table (`nr-epilepsy` `ep-6`). **`rabies` and `tetanus` return ZERO across all 25 decks**|\n\n### ⚠️ One source is UNREAD, and that is recorded rather than guessed\n- **Book Neurology ch.13, `CNS Infections` — printed 128–135 = PDF 139–146, 8 pages.** **Image-only**; reading it needs a page render, which was not authorised for this chapter. The book map records its figures as **unnumbered, with `Kernig sign` and `Brudzinski sign` labelled INSIDE the image.** **Everything in this chapter is the lecture's. Whatever the book adds is not here.**\n\n### And two source defects, noted and not corrected\n- **CSF CELL COUNTS ARE WRITTEN `/dl`** throughout the deck (`ci-6`, `ci-7`) — **transcribed as printed.**\n- **CASE 2'S CSF PROTEIN IS PRINTED `35gr/dl`** — **impossible as written**; read as **mg/dl** in `ci-10`. **Both are recorded; neither is silently repaired.**\n\nSrc: register verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js from disk. Absence probes run over all 25 caches in content/neuro/lectures/. Book range and figure note from content/neuro/book-map.md",
