        "body": "### What it is\n- **The definition:** a disorder characterised by **MULTIPLE SOMATIC COMPLAINTS REQUIRING MEDICAL ATTENTION**, but **NOT ASSOCIATED WITH ANY PHYSICAL DISORDER.**\n- *The deck titles the slide **SOMATIC SYMPTOM DISORDER** and subtitles it **(Somatization Disorder)** — the DSM-5 and DSM-IV names of the same entity, side by side.*\n\n### Epidemiology — every figure the slide prints\n|**Axis**|**Figure**|\n|---|---|\n|**Prevalence**|**estimated 4–6 %**, ⚠️ **but may be as high as 15 %**|\n|**Age**|**commonly appears in persons 20 to 30 years of age**|\n|**Sex**|**MALE = FEMALE**|\n|**⚠️ Medical students**|**occurs in about 3 PER CENT of medical students, usually IN THE FIRST TWO YEARS**|\n|**The typical patient**|**UNMARRIED · of LOWER SOCIOECONOMIC STATUS · LIVING IN A RURAL AREA**|\n\n- **⚠️ Three sex ratios, and they differ:** **male = female here** · **conversion disorder affects WOMEN more frequently** (`so-7`) · **body dysmorphic disorder is almost equal** (`so-9`). **All three are the deck's own.**\n- **⚠️ FIVE SLIDES OF THIS ENTITY ARE PICTURES.** The deck runs **one text slide, then THREE consecutive picture-only slides, then Management** — measured with `pdffonts` and `pdftotext` page by page, not assumed. **Whatever those three teach is not recoverable from the cache**, and the likeliest content is the diagnostic criteria, which **the deck otherwise prints for conversion disorder alone.** **Recorded in `so-13`, not guessed.**\n\nSrc: L3 sl. SOMATIC SYMPTOM DISORDER (Somatization Disorder), in full. The picture-slide measurement is of the PDF itself, per page",
