        "body": "### The eight-point plan, as the slide prints it\n|**Point**|**What it says**|\n|---|---|\n|**Who runs it**|**the PRIMARY CARE PRACTITIONER should DIRECT CARE**|\n|**How often**|**REGULARLY SCHEDULED VISITS EVERY 4–6 WEEKS**|\n|**How long**|**visits should be KEPT SHORT**|\n|**What happens in them**|**perform at least PART OF A PHYSICAL EXAMINATION at each visit**|\n|**⚠️ What does not**|**AVOID DIAGNOSTIC TESTS and OPERATIVE PROCEDURES unless CLEARLY INDICATED**|\n|**What to look for**|**SIGNS of disease, RATHER THAN BEING SYMPTOM-FOCUSED**|\n|**How to hear the symptom**|**understand symptoms in terms of EMOTIONAL COMMUNICATION rather than DISEASE**|\n|**Psychotherapy**|**GROUP PSYCHOTHERAPY provides SOCIAL SUPPORT and RELIEVES ANXIETY**|\n|**Pharmacotherapy**|**for UNDERLYING DEPRESSION OR ANXIETY** — ⚠️ **and for nothing else**|\n\n### The two clauses worth separating out\n- **⚠️ Scheduled, not symptom-driven:** and `so-12` gives the reason the slide leaves implicit — it **minimises the patient's need to develop new symptoms in order to receive care.**\n- **⚠️ It treats the comorbidity:** **pharmacotherapy is NOT for the somatization.** **No drug, class or dose is printed anywhere in the deck for it**, and the deck's own *Pharmacotherapy* slide adds only a **negative** — **placebo is NOT a useful technique for long-term help in these patients** (`so-12`).\n\n- *`ps-therapy` `th-6` already carries this chapter's group-psychotherapy match in its which-therapy-for-which-disorder table, sourced to this slide. Antidepressant and anxiolytic classes are `ps-pharm`. Neither is repeated here.*\n\nSrc: L3 sl. Management, in full · the Pharmacotherapy slide for the placebo clause. Group-psychotherapy cross-reference: `ps-therapy` `th-6`",
