        "h": "Undifferentiated somatoform disorder",
        "body": "### The milder form, and the one with the numbers\n- **What it is:** **a MILDER FORM of somatization disorder, which requires FEWER SYMPTOMS for diagnosis.**\n- **⚠️ THE FIGURE TO CARRY:** it is **30 TO 100 TIMES MORE PREVALENT** than **full-blown somatization disorder.**\n- **The deck's own example:** **a patient with CHEST PAIN and NO CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE.**\n- **Comorbidity:** with **other psychiatric conditions — DEPRESSION, ANXIETY, PERSONALITY DISORDER — in ABOUT 50 % of patients.**\n- **Treatment:** **SIMILAR TO THAT FOR SOMATIZATION DISORDER** (`so-5`). *No separate plan is printed.*\n\n- **⚠️ The two prevalences:** they do not sit easily together. Somatization disorder is given as **4–6 %, possibly 15 %** (`so-4`); this milder form as **30–100 times more prevalent** than that. **Both are the deck's, recorded as printed. It reconciles them nowhere.**\n\nSrc: L3 sl. Undifferentiated somatoform disorder, in full",
