        "h": "Incompatibility, and the four worked examples",
        "body": "### ⚠️ What is incompatibility — the deck asks, and answers with two words\n- **The slide's whole text:** *What is Incompatability---!!!!* · **Hoover's sign.** **Then the next slide is a picture.**\n- **The sign, from L12:** written out in full in `nr-hemi` `hem-2` — supine, the patient lifts one leg at a time; a **truly paralysed leg still presses the OPPOSITE HEEL DOWN**, so **failure to press = POSITIVE Hoover = functional.** **Not repeated here.**\n- **⚠️ And four more clues:** `hem-2` carries **four detectors of functional weakness that L3 never prints** — **improvement in strength with COACHING** · **GIVE-WAY weakness** · **inconsistency** (cannot extend the foot, but can walk on the toes) · **paralysis with NO other motor sign**, tone and reflexes unchanged.\n- *This is the second time in two chapters that a probe into another deck answered a question this one only asks.*\n\n### The four worked examples\n|**Example**|**What the deck says**|\n|---|---|\n|**ASTASIA-ABASIA**|**a STAGGERING ATAXIC GAIT with JERKS and THRASHING of the upper extremities**, often with **INABILITY TO STAND WITHOUT SUPPORT.** ⚠️ **The line that makes it: *a patient may not be able to walk, but can dance.***|\n|**PSEUDOSEIZURES**|**paroxysmal episodes of SEIZURE-LIKE BEHAVIOUR, WITHOUT the clinical features or the EEG findings of epilepsy.** ⚠️ **The four discriminators: NO SELF-HARM · LONG DURATION · SECONDARY GAIN · NO URINARY INCONTINENCE**|\n|**SENSORY SYMPTOMS**|**ANAESTHESIA · HYPAESTHESIA · PARAESTHESIA — in DISTRIBUTIONS THAT ARE NOT PHYSIOLOGIC.** The deck's example: **anaesthesia of ONE ENTIRE LIMB**|\n|**HYSTERICAL BLINDNESS**|**the PUPILS REACT TO LIGHT** — the whole slide, and the whole test|\n\n### ⚠️ Each example is the same argument\n- **The finding contradicts the anatomy.** A limb anaesthetic to its exact boundary follows no dermatome and no nerve; a pupil that reacts proves the **afferent limb is intact**; a gait that fails walking and succeeds dancing uses the **same muscles both times**. **That is criterion 2 of `so-7`.**\n\n- *`nr-epilepsy` `ep-3` carries the **full three-column seizure / syncope / pseudoseizure table**, whose own hardest discriminators are **DURATION**, **SLEEP ONSET** — a pseudoseizure **never arises from sleep** — and **SKIN COLOUR**. **L3 prints none of those three, and L4 prints none of L3's four.** **The two lists are complementary, and neither deck contains the other.***\n\nSrc: L3 sl. What is Incompatability---!!!! · Examples of conversion disorder — both in full. Hoover's sign and the four extra clues: L12 via `nr-hemi` `hem-2`. Pseudoseizure comparison: L4 via `nr-epilepsy` `ep-3`",
