        "h": "Factitious illness against malingering — two axes, not one",
        "body": "### Factitious illness — the three defining points\n- **1 —** **INTENTIONAL FEIGNING of PHYSICAL OR PSYCHOLOGICAL symptoms.**\n- **2 —** **the MOTIVATION for the behaviour is THE SICK ROLE.**\n- **3 —** **ABSENCE of an obvious EXTERNAL INCENTIVE** — no **economic gain**, no **avoidance of unpleasant duties.**\n\n### What that looks like\n- **The symptoms:** **INTENTIONALLY PRODUCED OR FEIGNED.**\n- **FALSE INFORMATION IS GIVEN INTENTIONALLY.**\n- **⚠️ Done consciously:** **the self-injurious behaviours or simulated somatic complaints are deliberate** — the patient **assumes a sick role to obtain the caring that comes with medical treatment.**\n- **⚠️ FACTITIOUS ILLNESS BY PROXY —** named by the deck and **not expanded**: **the symptoms are produced in ANOTHER PERSON, characteristically a child, by a carer who then presents them for medical attention** *(not taken from the course material; `Munchausen` returns ZERO across all 25 decks)*.\n\n### Malingering\n- **The goals are INTENTIONAL AND OBVIOUS —** **FINANCIAL COMPENSATION · AVOIDANCE OF DUTY OR SCHOOL · EVASION OF CRIMINAL PROSECUTION · OBTAINING OF DRUGS.**\n- **The distinguishing feature:** **the CONSCIOUS INTENT in the production of the symptoms.**\n- **Where it is met:** **MEDICOLEGAL** and **FORENSIC** populations.\n- **⚠️ AND THE LINE THE DECK PUTS LAST: MALINGERING IS NOT A MENTAL ILLNESS.**\n\n### ⚠️ The three-way table the deck never draws\n|**Axis**|**Somatoform / conversion**|**Factitious illness**|**Malingering**|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|**Is the symptom produced consciously?**|**NO** — not under conscious control|**YES** — intentionally produced or feigned|**YES** — conscious intent|\n|**What is the motivation?**|**not stated by the deck**|**THE SICK ROLE**|**an EXTERNAL INCENTIVE**|\n|**External incentive present?**|**not stated**|**ABSENT — that is criterion 3**|**PRESENT, and obvious**|\n|**A mental illness?**|**yes** — it is in the classification of `so-3`|**yes** — the deck teaches it here|**⚠️ NO, explicitly**|\n\n- **⚠️ TWO AXES, NOT ONE.** **Consciousness separates the somatoform group from the other two; INCENTIVE then separates factitious illness from malingering.** *Neither axis alone does the job, and the deck states both without ever putting them side by side.*\n- *`nr-hemi` `hem-2` draws the same conscious/unconscious line at the bedside for a functional hemiplegia, and gives the five clues that detect it (`so-8`).*\n\nSrc: L3 sl. FACTITIOUS ILLNESS ×2 · Malingering — all in full. Factitious illness by proxy is named by the deck and the expansion is tagged. The three-way table is assembled; the deck prints no such comparison",
