        "h": "General principles, and the wisdom of doing less",
        "body": "### The frame\n- **⚠️ The slide opens with the oath:** ***\"Never do harm\"* — the Hippocratic Oath.** *In a chapter whose central risk is iatrogenic investigation, that is the argument, not decoration.*\n\n### Who, how often, and how much\n|**Principle**|**And the reason the slide gives for it**|\n|---|---|\n|**A SINGLE CLINICIAN**|management of the somatizing patient **is best done by one**|\n|**⚠️ REFERRALS SPARINGLY**|they **add the impression that the problem is BOTH PHYSICAL AND SEVERE**|\n|**REGULAR, BRIEF VISITS**|**MINIMIZES the patient's need to DEVELOP MORE NEW SYMPTOMS IN ORDER TO RECEIVE CARE**, and **reminds the patient of the physician's AVAILABILITY AND CONCERN**|\n|**LOOK FOR SIGNS of disease**|**rather than being SYMPTOM-FOCUSED**|\n|**Understand symptoms as EMOTIONAL COMMUNICATION**|**rather than as disease**|\n|**⚠️ THE WORKUP IS LIMITED**|although **physical illness MUST BE RULED OUT** — this **avoids unnecessary investigations and treatment**, and **avoids reinforcing the idea that the problem is ONLY PHYSICAL**|\n\n### How to give the diagnosis\n- **⚠️ DISCUSS THE DIAGNOSIS CAUTIOUSLY.** **Telling a somatizing patient that *\"it's all in your head\"* is NOT AT ALL USEFUL.**\n- **Why the caution:** it **DECREASES THE STIGMA attached to a PSYCHOGENIC AETIOLOGY.**\n- **⚠️ The sentence to remember:** **they \"SOMATIZE\" rather than \"PSYCHOLOGIZE.\"**\n- **AIM FOR ALLIANCE AND REASSURANCE.**\n- **Do not insist:** the patient need not see their case **AT FIRST as \"psychological\"** — **it may well take a while before they are willing to consider the possibility of psychological factors.**\n\n### Pharmacotherapy — the whole slide\n- **⚠️ Placebo:** **THE USE OF PLACEBO IS NOT A USEFUL TECHNIQUE for long-term help in these patients.**\n- **⚠️ AND THAT IS ALL THE SLIDE SAYS.** The heading is *Pharmacotherapy* and **it prints one negative and no drug at all.** The only positive indication in the deck is `so-5`'s — **for an underlying depression or anxiety.** **No agent, class, dose or duration appears anywhere in L3.**\n\nSrc: L3 sl. General Principles · General Principles (cont.) · Pharmacotherapy — all three in full",
