        "body": "### ⚠️⚠️ ELEVEN OF L3's FORTY SLIDES CARRY NO TEXT AT ALL\n*Measured page by page on the PDF with `pdffonts` and `pdftotext -layout`, not assumed. **Zero fonts means the slide is an IMAGE — nothing is vector-outlined and nothing is hidden from the extractor.** Four more slides carry between one and five words.*\n\n|**Pages**|**Where they fall**|**What is lost**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**p.10, 11, 12**|**INSIDE somatic symptom disorder** — between its one text slide and Management|⚠️ **three consecutive slides.** The deck prints **diagnostic criteria for conversion disorder and for no other entity**, so these are the likeliest home of the missing criteria|\n|**p.22–26**|**THE WHOLE OF HYPOCHONDRIASIS** — the heading `(Hypochondriasis)` alone on p.22, then **four blank-of-text slides**|⚠️⚠️ **an entire STARRED disorder.** Supplied and tagged in `so-9`|\n|**p.19**|**immediately after `What is Incompatability---!!!!` / `Hoover's sign`**|**the Hoover's sign figure.** ✅ **PAID ANYWAY** — `nr-hemi` `hem-2` writes the sign out in full from L12|\n|**p.3, 15, 21, 31**|title area · before conversion disorder · after its examples · before *Obstacles of treatment*|**section-break or illustrative slides; no heading is orphaned by them**|\n\n- **⚠️ THE HONEST STATEMENT: this chapter is written from the 29 slides that carry text.** Everything in it is sourced or tagged; **what those eleven slides teach is not in it.**\n\n### ⚠️ One source is UNREAD, and this is recorded rather than guessed\n- **Book Psychiatry ch.5 —** `Somatic Symptoms and related disorders`, **printed 215–221 = PDF 227–233, 7 pages. Image-only**; reading it needs a page render, which was not authorised for this chapter. ⚠️ **It is the single most valuable unread source in the module for this chapter**, because it is the one place that can replace `so-9`'s tagged hypochondriasis and, plausibly, the three lost criteria slides.\n\n### §14.5 register — what this chapter POINTS at rather than repeating\n|**Fact**|**Lives in**|**Verified?**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**HOOVER'S SIGN**, and four more clues to functional weakness|`nr-hemi` `hem-2` (L12)|✅ read from disk|\n|**LA BELLE INDIFFERENCE**, defined|`ps-symptom` `sy-3`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Conversion against MALINGERING** at the bedside|`nr-hemi` `hem-2`|✅ read from disk|\n|**PSEUDOSEIZURE** against true seizure and syncope, the full table|`nr-epilepsy` `ep-3`|✅ read from disk|\n|**BODY DYSMORPHIC DISORDER's DSM-5 home**, and BDD against OCD|`ps-ocd` `oc-2`/`oc-6`/`oc-10` · `ps-anxiety` `ax-2`|✅ read from disk|\n|**GROUP PSYCHOTHERAPY** in the which-therapy-for-which-disorder table|`ps-therapy` `th-6`|✅ **already points back at this deck**|\n|**Antidepressant and anxiolytic classes** for the comorbidity|`ps-pharm`|✅ written|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Three were nearly filled:** `Hoover's sign`, `la belle indifference` and the conversion-against-malingering line are all **named and not defined by L3** — and **all three are already written in this module, from other decks.** *The fifteenth payment of **read the slide before declaring a gap**, and the first where one probe recovered three separate fills at once.*\n\n### ⚠️ Verified absences — probed across all 25 cached decks\n|**What**|**Probe result**|\n|---|---|\n|**PAIN DISORDER**|listed in the DSM-IV classification and **taught nowhere**; `pain disorder` returns **one hit in 25 decks — that list**|\n|**SOMATOFORM DISORDER NOS**|**same** — listed, never expanded|\n|**ILLNESS ANXIETY DISORDER**|**ZERO across all 25 decks.** DSM-5's replacement for hypochondriasis is never named|\n|**MUNCHAUSEN / MUNCHAUSEN BY PROXY**|**ZERO.** The deck writes **`Factitious illness by proxy`** and does not expand it; the expansion in `so-10` is tagged|\n|**HISTRIONIC PERSONALITY**|**⚠️ one hit, MISSPELLED `Hysterionic`, on this deck's conversion slide.** `histrion` spelled correctly returns **ZERO across all 25 decks** — *the `ostio-` trap again: probe the misspelling too*|\n|**ANY DRUG for somatization**|**none.** The *Pharmacotherapy* slide prints **one negative** — placebo is not useful long-term — **and no agent** (`so-12`)|\n\n### And one framing defect, recorded not corrected\n- **⚠️ Two frames at once:** **the deck teaches DSM-IV while titling itself with the DSM-5 name** (`so-3`). **Both are transcribed as printed.**\n\nSrc: page-by-page measurement of `Semester 8/Neuro/Theoritical/PPT/L3) Somatization.pdf`. Register verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js read from disk. Absence probes over all 25 caches in content/neuro/lectures/. Book range from content/neuro/book-map.md",
