        "h": "The developing brain — 100 billion neurons and the pruning paradox",
        "body": "### The starting point — a 100-billion-neuron foundation\n- **At birth:** **~100 BILLION NEURONS** — **nearly the full population the brain will EVER have.** **The cellular foundation is already in place.**\n- **⚠️ So growth is not cell count:** the brain's **true growth lies in the EXPLOSIVE EXPANSION OF SYNAPTIC CONNECTIONS**, which is what enables **LEARNING, EMOTION and SELF-REGULATION.**\n\n### Childhood architecture — connectivity, then refinement\n|**Stage**|**What happens**|\n|---|---|\n|**THE 1,000-TRILLION NETWORK**|**by AGE 3** the brain forms **roughly 1,000 TRILLION SYNAPSES** through **rapid branching** — ⚠️ **MORE THAN IT WILL EVER NEED**|\n|**⚠️ THE PRUNING PARADOX**|***\"Use it or lose it\"*** — **efficient circuits STRENGTHEN while unused connections are DISCARDED**, **especially during AGES 2–3 and ADOLESCENCE**|\n|**THE NEURODEVELOPMENTAL LINK**|**when OVERPRODUCTION and PRUNING FAIL TO BALANCE, ABNORMAL CONNECTIVITY EMERGES** — linked to **AUTISM, ADHD and other disorders** affecting **social, cognitive and communication functions**|\n\n- **⚠️ This is the deck's only pathophysiology**, and it is the frame for everything after it: **the neurodevelopmental disorders in `ch-2` are presented as failures of the same two processes** — overproduction and pruning — **not as separate diseases with separate mechanisms.**\n- **⚠️ The two vulnerable windows are named:** **ages 2–3** and **adolescence.** *No mechanism, molecule or gene is given for the imbalance itself; the deck states it and moves on.*\n\nSrc: L14 sl. The Starting Point: A 100 Billion Neuron Foundation · Childhood Architecture: Connectivity and Refinement — both in full",
