        "body": "### The eight categories DSM-5 puts under Neurodevelopmental Disorders\n|**#**|**Category**|**Where it is here**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1**|**INTELLECTUAL DISORDERS**|`ch-3`|\n|**2**|**COMMUNICATION DISORDERS**|`ch-4`|\n|**3**|**AUTISM SPECTRUM DISORDER**|`ch-5`|\n|**4**|**ATTENTION-DEFICIT / HYPERACTIVITY DISORDER**|`ch-9`, `ch-10`|\n|**5**|**SPECIFIC LEARNING DISORDERS**|`ch-6`|\n|**6**|**MOTOR DISORDERS**|`ch-7`|\n|**7**|**TIC DISORDERS**|`ch-8`|\n|**8**|**OTHER NEURODEVELOPMENTAL DISORDERS**|⚠️ **named and never expanded**|\n\n- **⚠️ Seven of its own eight:** the deck **teaches all seven and leaves the eighth as a catch-all.** *Every one is covered below, which makes this the module's most completely-taught deck.*\n\n### The causes — a six-spoke wheel, and no more than the names\n- **NUTRITIONAL FACTORS.**\n- **SOCIAL DEPRIVATION.**\n- **PHYSICAL TRAUMA.**\n- **INFECTIOUS DISEASES.**\n- **GENETIC.**\n- **IMMUNE DISORDERS.**\n- **⚠️ Names only:** the slide is **a diagram of six labelled spokes** around the words *Causes of Neurodevelopmental Disorders*, **and that is the entire slide.** **No example, mechanism, relative weight or age of exposure is given for ANY of the six.** *Nothing is supplied — six aetiological lists written from memory is not a gap-fill.*\n\nSrc: L14 sl. The DSM-5 categorizes the following disorders under Neurodevelopmental Disorders · Causes of Neurodevelopmental Disorders — both in full, the second being a labelled diagram",
