        "h": "Intellectual disability — three criteria, four levels",
        "body": "### The three criteria — all must be met\n*The disorder has **onset during the DEVELOPMENTAL PERIOD** and includes **BOTH intellectual AND adaptive functioning deficits** in **CONCEPTUAL, SOCIAL and PRACTICAL domains.***\n\n|**Criterion**|**What it requires**|\n|---|---|\n|**A — INTELLECTUAL**|deficits in **REASONING · PROBLEM SOLVING · PLANNING · ABSTRACT THINKING · JUDGMENT · ACADEMIC LEARNING · LEARNING FROM EXPERIENCE**. ⚠️ **Confirmed by BOTH clinical assessment AND individualized, standardized intelligence testing** — both, not either|\n|**B — ADAPTIVE**|deficits that **result in FAILURE TO MEET DEVELOPMENTAL AND SOCIOCULTURAL STANDARDS for PERSONAL INDEPENDENCE and SOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY.** ⚠️ **Without ongoing support** they **limit functioning in ONE OR MORE activities of daily life** — **communication, social participation, independent living** — **ACROSS MULTIPLE ENVIRONMENTS: home, school, work, community**|\n|**C — TIMING**|**onset of the intellectual AND adaptive deficits DURING THE DEVELOPMENTAL PERIOD**|\n\n- **⚠️ Criterion B:** **the one most often misremembered.** The deficit must limit daily life **across MULTIPLE environments**, and the qualifier **\"without ongoing support\"** means **a supported patient who functions is still affected.**\n\n### The four levels, by IQ\n|**Level**|**IQ**|\n|---|---|\n|**MILD**|**50 to 70**|\n|**MODERATE**|**35 to 49**|\n|**SEVERE**|**20 to 34**|\n|**PROFOUND**|**under 20**|\n\n- **⚠️ Two severity frames:** **IQ on this slide, ADAPTIVE FUNCTIONING in criterion B.** **The deck prints both and reconciles them nowhere** — *recorded as printed.*\n- *The **Pediatrics** module teaches the same entity from its own deck, under **intellectual subnormality**, with the **ten adaptive skills** and an **onset-before-18** clause that this deck does not print. **Different module, same disorder; neither is repeated in the other.***\n\nSrc: L14 sl. Intellectual disability (intellectual developmental disorder) Diagnostic Criteria · Levels of intellectual disability — both in full",
