        "id": "ch-5",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Autism spectrum disorder — two domains, both required",
        "body": "### The number\n- **Prevalence:** **ALMOST 6.6 PER 1,000 CHILDREN.** *The deck's only ASD figure — no sex ratio, no age of diagnosis, no trend.*\n\n### Criterion 1 — persistent deficits in SOCIAL COMMUNICATION AND SOCIAL INTERACTION, across multiple contexts\n|**Sub-item**|**The deficit**|\n|---|---|\n|**a**|**deficits in SOCIAL-EMOTIONAL RECIPROCITY**|\n|**b**|**deficits in NONVERBAL COMMUNICATIVE BEHAVIOURS used for social interaction**|\n|**c**|**deficits in DEVELOPING, MAINTAINING and UNDERSTANDING RELATIONSHIPS**|\n\n- **⚠️ Part of the criterion:** ***\"across multiple contexts\"*** **is not a qualifier** — the same clause `ch-3`'s criterion B uses for intellectual disability.\n\n### Criterion 2 — restricted, repetitive patterns of BEHAVIOUR, INTERESTS or ACTIVITIES\n|**Sub-item**|**The pattern**|\n|---|---|\n|**a**|**STEREOTYPED OR REPETITIVE MOTOR MOVEMENTS, USE OF OBJECTS, or SPEECH**|\n|**b**|**INSISTENCE ON SAMENESS**, **INFLEXIBLE ADHERENCE TO ROUTINES**, or **RITUALIZED PATTERNS of verbal or nonverbal behaviour**|\n|**c**|**HIGHLY RESTRICTED, FIXATED INTERESTS** that are **ABNORMAL IN INTENSITY OR FOCUS**|\n|**d**|**⚠️ HYPER- OR HYPO-REACTIVITY TO SENSORY INPUT**, or **UNUSUAL INTEREST IN SENSORY ASPECTS of the environment**|\n\n- **⚠️ Sub-item 2d:** the one most often forgotten, and the one **DSM-5 added** — **sensory reactivity is a DIAGNOSTIC feature of autism, not an associated one**, and it runs **BOTH ways**, hyper- and hypo-.\n- **⚠️ TWO DOMAINS, AND BOTH ARE REQUIRED.** A child with criterion 1 alone and no restricted or repetitive behaviour is **social (pragmatic) communication disorder** (`ch-4`), not autism.\n- *`ps-symptom` `sy-4` defines **STEREOTYPY** in the mental-state examination — **a repeated purposeless movement, with no model to copy** — which is sub-item 2a's word. **Not repeated here.** The **stereotypic movement disorder** that shares it is `ch-7`.*\n- **⚠️ No management:** **the deck gives none for autism at all** — no behavioural programme, no drug, no service. *`ps-devices` `dv-7` records that **commercial clinics heavily advertise transcranial stimulation OFF-LABEL for autism**, the module's only other appearance of the word.*\n\nSrc: L14 sl. Autism Spectrum Disorder · 2. Restricted, repetitive patterns of behavior, interests, or activities — both in full, including every lettered sub-item",
