        "id": "ch-6",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Specific learning disorder — six symptoms, three types",
        "body": "### Who is diagnosed\n- **⚠️ MORE FREQUENTLY IN BOYS THAN GIRLS —** and the deck gives the figures: **in 2013, 9 % of boys and 6 % of girls aged 6 to 17.**\n\n### The DSM-5 criterion — and its two hard qualifiers\n- **The criterion:** **difficulties LEARNING AND USING ACADEMIC SKILLS**, indicated by **AT LEAST ONE** of the six symptoms below.\n- **⚠️ QUALIFIER 1 — DURATION:** the symptoms must have **PERSISTED FOR AT LEAST 6 MONTHS.**\n- **⚠️ QUALIFIER 2 — AND THIS IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS:** **DESPITE THE PROVISION OF INTERVENTIONS THAT TARGET THOSE DIFFICULTIES.** **A child who has not been taught, or not been helped, is not yet diagnosable.**\n\n### The six symptoms\n|**#**|**Symptom**|**Domain it belongs to**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1**|**INACCURATE, or SLOW AND EFFORTFUL, WORD READING**|reading|\n|**2**|**DIFFICULTY UNDERSTANDING THE MEANING of what is read**|reading|\n|**3**|**DIFFICULTIES WITH SPELLING**|written expression|\n|**4**|**DIFFICULTIES WITH WRITTEN EXPRESSION**|written expression|\n|**5**|**DIFFICULTIES MASTERING NUMBER SENSE, NUMBER FACTS or CALCULATION**|mathematics|\n|**6**|**DIFFICULTIES WITH MATHEMATICAL REASONING**|mathematics|\n\n### The three types — the specifiers\n- **1 — WITH IMPAIRMENT IN READING.**\n- **2 — WITH IMPAIRMENT IN WRITTEN EXPRESSION.**\n- **3 — WITH IMPAIRMENT IN MATHEMATICS.**\n\n- **⚠️ Two symptoms per type:** **the six map two-to-one onto the three types**, which is why the deck prints both lists — **the symptoms establish the diagnosis, the types specify it.**\n- *The deck names **no treatment** for specific learning disorder — no educational intervention, no accommodation, no drug.*\n\nSrc: L14 sl. Specific Learning Disorder · 3. Difficulties with spelling … / Types of SLD — both in full. The symptom-to-type mapping column is assembled; the deck prints the two lists separately",
