        "id": "ch-9",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "ADHD — the DSM-5 criteria in full",
        "body": "### The core statement, and the counting rule\n- **ADHD:** **a PERSISTENT PATTERN of INATTENTION and/or HYPERACTIVITY-IMPULSIVITY** that **INTERFERES WITH FUNCTIONING OR DEVELOPMENT.**\n- **⚠️ \"AND/OR\" IS THE WHOLE CLASSIFICATION** — either domain alone suffices, which is why the disorder has an inattentive, a hyperactive-impulsive and a combined presentation.\n- **⚠️ The threshold:** **identical for both domains — SIX OR MORE symptoms**, persisting **AT LEAST 6 MONTHS**, to a degree **INCONSISTENT WITH DEVELOPMENTAL LEVEL** and **NEGATIVELY IMPACTING DIRECTLY on SOCIAL and ACADEMIC / OCCUPATIONAL ACTIVITIES.**\n\n### INATTENTION — the nine\n|**#**|**Symptom**|\n|---|---|\n|**a**|**often FAILS TO GIVE CLOSE ATTENTION TO DETAILS**, or **makes CARELESS MISTAKES** in schoolwork, at work, or during other activities|\n|**b**|**often has DIFFICULTY SUSTAINING ATTENTION** in tasks or play activities|\n|**c**|**often DOES NOT SEEM TO LISTEN when spoken to directly**|\n|**d**|**often DOES NOT FOLLOW THROUGH ON INSTRUCTIONS** and **FAILS TO FINISH** schoolwork, chores or duties in the workplace|\n|**e**|**often has DIFFICULTY ORGANIZING TASKS AND ACTIVITIES**|\n|**f**|**often AVOIDS, DISLIKES or IS RELUCTANT to engage in tasks that require SUSTAINED MENTAL EFFORT**|\n|**g**|**often LOSES THINGS necessary for tasks or activities**|\n|**h**|**is often EASILY DISTRACTED BY EXTRANEOUS STIMULI**|\n|**i**|**is often FORGETFUL IN DAILY ACTIVITIES**|\n\n### HYPERACTIVITY AND IMPULSIVITY — the nine\n|**#**|**Symptom**|**Which half**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**a**|**often FIDGETS with or TAPS HANDS OR FEET, or SQUIRMS IN SEAT**|hyperactivity|\n|**b**|**often LEAVES SEAT** in situations when remaining seated is expected|hyperactivity|\n|**c**|**often RUNS ABOUT OR CLIMBS** where it is inappropriate|hyperactivity|\n|**d**|**often UNABLE TO PLAY or engage in leisure activities QUIETLY**|hyperactivity|\n|**e**|**is often \"ON THE GO\", acting as if \"DRIVEN BY A MOTOR\"** — experienced by others as **RESTLESS or DIFFICULT TO KEEP UP WITH**|hyperactivity|\n|**f**|**often TALKS EXCESSIVELY**|hyperactivity|\n|**g**|**often BLURTS OUT AN ANSWER before a question has been completed**|**impulsivity**|\n|**h**|**often has DIFFICULTY WAITING HIS OR HER TURN**|**impulsivity**|\n|**i**|**often INTERRUPTS OR INTRUDES ON OTHERS**|**impulsivity**|\n\n- **⚠️ One criterion, two behaviours:** the deck's own ordering separates them — **a–f are HYPERACTIVITY, g–i are IMPULSIVITY.** *The split is assembled here; the slide prints the nine as one list.*\n- *`ps-symptom` `sy-8` places **DISTRACTIBILITY** — inability to sustain attention — in the mental-state examination, with **mania, depression and ADHD** as its three causes. **That is the differential this criterion sits inside**, and it is not repeated here.*\n\nSrc: L14 sl. DSM-5 criteria of ADHD, and the three continuation slides — all four in full, every lettered symptom of both domains",
