        "id": "ch-10",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "ADHD management — and the module's only regional pharmacology",
        "body": "### Pharmacological — stimulants and non-stimulants\n|**#**|**Agent**|**Class**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1**|**METHYLPHENIDATE**|**STIMULANT** — ⚠️ **named and nothing more; the slide gives no mechanism, dose or adverse effect for it**|\n|**2**|**ATOMOXETINE**|**NON-STIMULANT**|\n|**3**|**GUANFACINE · CLONIDINE**|**ALPHA-2 ADRENERGIC AGONISTS**|\n\n### ⚠️ Atomoxetine — the deck's one worked mechanism, and it is an argument about abuse\n- **What it is:** a **SELECTIVE NOREPINEPHRINE REUPTAKE INHIBITOR.**\n- **In the PREFRONTAL CORTEX:** **inhibiting NET increases BOTH DOPAMINE AND NORADRENALINE** — because the prefrontal cortex is **DEFICIENT IN DAT**, so **NET clears the dopamine there.**\n- **⚠️ In the NUCLEUS ACCUMBENS:** **NO NE or DA increase**, because there is **LESS NET** — **and therefore NO ABUSE POTENTIAL.**\n- **⚠️ The module's only regional pharmacology.** *It explains why a noradrenergic drug raises dopamine where the therapeutic effect is, and does not raise it where the reward is.*\n\n### The two alpha-2 agonists are not interchangeable\n|**Agent**|**Selectivity**|\n|---|---|\n|**GUANFACINE**|**SELECTIVE agonist at α2A**|\n|**CLONIDINE**|**NONSELECTIVE agonist at α2A, α2B and α2C**|\n\n- **⚠️ Why both are listed:** **that single selectivity contrast is the whole reason.** *No dose, frequency, adverse effect or contraindication is printed for any of the four agents — and none is supplied.*\n\n### Non-pharmacological — four\n- **PARENT-TRAINING / EDUCATION PROGRAMMES.**\n- **BEHAVIOUR THERAPY.**\n- **ENVIRONMENTAL MODIFICATIONS.**\n- **NEUROFEEDBACK TRAINING.**\n\n- **⚠️ The only management in the deck.** **Intellectual disability, the communication disorders, autism, specific learning disorder, the motor disorders and the tic disorders are all taught WITHOUT any treatment at all.**\n- *⚠️ **NEUROFEEDBACK is written out in full in `ps-devices` `dv-9`**, from L18: the **ADHD protocol is DECREASE high-amplitude THETA** (daydreaming, inattention) and **INCREASE BETA** (active processing), with **clinical efficacy as an ADJUNCTIVE, NON-PHARMACOLOGICAL option for paediatric ADHD.** **Not repeated here.** The deck's closing **Brain Map (QEEG)** slide is that assessment, and it carries **three words and a picture.***\n- *Stimulant and antidepressant classes in general are `ps-pharm`; **behaviour therapy** is `ps-therapy`, whose `th-10` records that **operant conditioning is the mechanism `dv-9` says neurofeedback relies on.***\n\nSrc: L14 sl. Management: Pharmacologic treatment · 2) Atomoxetine (non-stimulants) · Nonpharmacological treatment · Brain Map (QEEG) — all in full. Neurofeedback protocol: L18 via `ps-devices` `dv-9`",
