        "h": "What this chapter pays, and what child psychiatry here does not contain",
        "body": "### ✅ What this chapter PAYS — a §14.5 row that was waiting for it\n- **Who filed it:** **`ps-devices` `dv-10` addressed an ADHD row to this chapter by name**, because **`dv-9`'s theta/beta neurofeedback protocol and `dv-7`'s off-label marketing list both turn on ADHD** and L18 teaches neither the disorder nor its drugs. **PAID IN FULL: `ch-9` gives the DSM-5 criteria complete, `ch-10` gives all four agents and both treatment arms.**\n\n### What this chapter POINTS at rather than repeating\n|**Fact**|**Lives in**|**Verified?**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Tics — the phenomenology, and the ONLY-suppressible-movement test**|`nr-movement` `mv-10` (L3)|✅ read from disk|\n|**Tourette's typical onset 2–13, male predominance**|`nr-movement` `mv-10`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Tics against OCD compulsions**, and the **TIC-RELATED specifier**|`ps-ocd` `oc-6` and `oc-5` (L8)|✅ read from disk|\n|**STEREOTYPY as a mental-state sign**, against echolalia and echopraxia|`ps-symptom` `sy-4`|✅ read from disk|\n|**DISTRACTIBILITY** and its three causes — mania, depression, ADHD|`ps-symptom` `sy-8`|✅ read from disk|\n|**EEG NEUROFEEDBACK — the theta/beta ADHD protocol in full**|`ps-devices` `dv-9` (L18)|✅ read from disk|\n|**OPERANT CONDITIONING**, the mechanism neurofeedback relies on|`ps-therapy` `th-10`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Stimulant and antidepressant classes generally**|`ps-pharm`|✅ written|\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ THE SYLLABUS-LEVEL FINDING: child psychiatry here IS the neurodevelopmental disorders, and nothing else\n*Every probe below was run over all 25 cached decks.*\n\n|**Topic**|**Hits**|\n|---|---|\n|**OPPOSITIONAL DEFIANT DISORDER**|**ZERO**|\n|**CONDUCT DISORDER**|**ZERO**|\n|**ENURESIS · ENCOPRESIS**|**ZERO**|\n|**SEPARATION ANXIETY**|**ZERO**|\n|**ATTACHMENT** (and attachment disorders)|**ZERO**|\n|**CHILD ABUSE / MALTREATMENT**|**ZERO**|\n|**SELECTIVE (ELECTIVE) MUTISM**|**ZERO**|\n|**CHILDHOOD DEPRESSION, childhood anxiety, paediatric bipolar**|**no deck treats any of them as a child entity**|\n|**SCHOOL REFUSAL**|**ONE hit — `ps-ocd`'s paediatric complications row**, not a disorder in its own right|\n\n- **⚠️ Where they would sit:** **the deck's own eighth category, *OTHER NEURODEVELOPMENTAL DISORDERS*** — **named and never expanded** (`ch-2`).\n\n### ⚠️ Verified absences inside what IS taught\n|**What**|**Probe result**|\n|---|---|\n|**RETT SYNDROME**|**ZERO across all 25 decks.** ⚠️ *All three apparent hits are the string `rett` inside **Tourette** — the misspelling trap run in reverse: **check what a substring actually matched.***|\n|**FRAGILE X**|**ZERO**|\n|**DOWN SYNDROME**|**ONE hit, and not here** — L13 lists it as a **risk factor for dementia** (`ps-geri`, not yet written)|\n|**ANY DOSE**|**none.** Four ADHD agents are named; **no dose, frequency, adverse effect or contraindication for any of them.** **Deliberately not supplied**|\n|**MANAGEMENT of six of the seven disorders**|**ADHD is the only one with a treatment slide.** Intellectual disability, the communication disorders, autism, specific learning disorder, the motor disorders and the tic disorders are **all taught without any management at all**|\n|**Methylphenidate's mechanism**|**not printed** — the slide names it and expands **atomoxetine** instead (`ch-10`)|\n\n### ⚠️ One source is UNREAD, and this is recorded rather than guessed\n- **Book Psychiatry ch.6, `Child Psychiatry` — printed 222–227 = PDF 234–239, 6 pages.** **Image-only**; reading it needs a page render, which was not authorised for this chapter. The book map records it as opening on **neurodevelopmental disorders / intellectual disability**, so it likely parallels rather than extends the deck — **but that is an inference and nothing in this chapter rests on it.**\n\n### And the deck's own picture slides — measured, and this time almost none\n- **⚠️ Almost no pictures:** **only ONE of L14's 29 slides carries no text** (the last), and **one more carries three words** — the closing **`Brain Map (QEEG)`** slide, which is the assessment `ps-devices` `dv-9` describes. **Measured with `pdffonts` and `pdftotext -layout` page by page.** *Contrast `ps-somato`, where eleven of forty slides were pictures.*\n\nSrc: register verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js read from disk, section by section. Absence probes over all 25 caches in content/neuro/lectures/. Page measurement of the L14 PDF itself. Book range from content/neuro/book-map.md",
