        "h": "Dementia defined, and what this chapter's title does not have",
        "body": "### The word, and what it is not\n- **Origin:** **\"DEMENTIA\" is of LATIN origin and means *DEVOID OF MIND*.**\n- **What it describes:** **a PERSISTENT STATE of SERIOUS COGNITIVE, FUNCTIONAL AND EMOTIONAL DETERIORATION** — **FROM A PREVIOUSLY HIGHER LEVEL OF FUNCTIONING.**\n- **⚠️ The contrast the deck insists on:** **it should NOT be confused with MENTAL RETARDATION**, which denotes **DEFICIENT COGNITIVE DEVELOPMENT BEFORE THE AGE OF 18 YEARS.**\n- **⚠️ Direction, not severity:** **dementia is a LOSS from a level once held; intellectual disability is a level NEVER REACHED.** *`ps-child` `ch-3` teaches the second, with its DSM-5 criteria and IQ bands. Not repeated here.*\n\n### The deck's own three titles for the same territory\n- **All three head the opening slide:** **ORGANIC BRAIN SYNDROME · MILD AND MAJOR COGNITIVE DISORDER · DEMENTIA.** *The deck uses **dementia** throughout and never returns to the other two.*\n- **⚠️ Two frames at once:** **`mild` and `major cognitive disorder` are the DSM-5 names**, and **the deck names them once and teaches the older term instead** — the same pattern `ps-somato` `so-3` records for the DSM-IV somatoform disorders. *Recorded, not corrected.*\n\n### ⚠️ And a scope note this chapter has to make about itself\n- **The mismatch:** **this chapter is titled *Geriatric Psychiatry* and the deck it is written from is titled *Dementia and Delirium*.**\n- **⚠️ The probe:** **`geriatric` returns ZERO across all 25 cached decks.** **There is no geriatric-psychiatry teaching in the module** — no late-life depression as an entity, no elder abuse, no prescribing in the elderly.\n- **What IS here** is **dementia in full**, which is the overlap. **Delirium is `nr-delirium`**, from the same deck's second half. **The seam is the deck's own, at its *Delirium* title slide, and nothing is reordered.**\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Organic Brain Syndrome / Mild And Major Cognitive Disorder / Dementia, in full. The `geriatric` probe was run over all 25 caches in content/neuro/lectures/",
        "qs": []
