        "id": "ge-2",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "The two ladders — memory, and everything else",
        "body": "### Memory decline — three stages, and the deck gives an example for each\n|**Stage**|**What is lost**|**The deck's own examples**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**INITIALLY**|**LEARNING OF NEW INFORMATION**|**who they spoke to on the telephone earlier that day** · **what they had for breakfast that day**|\n|**AS THE DISEASE PROGRESSES**|**unable to recall PREVIOUSLY LEARNED information**|**names of famous people** · **local geography**|\n|**IN ADVANCED STAGES**|**may be unable to RECOGNISE EVEN CLOSE RELATIVES** — and **in the final stage may not be able to say WHO THEY THEMSELVES ARE**|—|\n\n- **⚠️ The order is the examinable part:** **NEW learning fails FIRST, old memory second, identity last.** *That is why `ps-symptom` `sy-8` files **recent amnesia** as **the main manifestation in dementia** and treats it as a marker of **organicity**.*\n\n### Decline in other cognitive abilities — the same three stages\n|**Stage**|**What is lost**|**The deck's own examples**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**INITIALLY**|**unable to do RELATIVELY COMPLICATED tasks they could previously do**|**cooking different items simultaneously** · **financial transactions involving filling forms**|\n|**AS THE ILLNESS PROGRESSES**|**need ASSISTANCE even for relatively SIMPLE tasks**|**paying bills by cash** · **choosing items in the shop**|\n|**IN ADVANCED STAGES**|**unable to do ANY cognitive activity EVEN WITH ASSISTANCE**|—|\n\n- **⚠️ Two parallel ladders:** the deck runs memory and executive function on **the same three-stage scale**, and **both sets of examples are financial** — *filling forms* early, *paying cash* late. **The task that survives longest is the one with the fewest steps.**\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Memory decline in dementia · Decline in other cognitive abilities — both in full, every example",
