        "id": "ge-7",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Alzheimer's disease — four gates and six domains",
        "body": "### What it is\n- **The commonest:** **AD is the MOST COMMON FORM of dementia, accounting for AROUND TWO-THIRDS OF CASES.** *Against the 65–85 % of `ge-6`; both printed.*\n- **What it does:** **causes a GRADUAL DECLINE IN COGNITIVE ABILITIES**, **often beginning with MEMORY LOSS — \"RECENT AMNESIA\".**\n\n### The diagnosis — four gates, then the domains\n|**Gate**|**What it requires**|\n|---|---|\n|**1**|**GRADUAL ONSET of symptoms**|\n|**2**|**⚠️ CLEAR CONSCIOUSNESS** — *the single feature that separates it from delirium at the bedside (`ge-10`, and `nr-delirium`)*|\n|**3**|**IRREVERSIBLE**|\n|**4**|**ONE OR MORE ACQUIRED SIGNIFICANT IMPAIRMENTS — with INDEPENDENCE LOST — in the cognitive domains below**|\n\n### The six cognitive domains, each with its deficit named\n|**Domain**|**The deficit**|\n|---|---|\n|**MEMORY**|**AMNESIA**|\n|**LANGUAGE**|**APHASIA**|\n|**EXECUTION OF PURPOSEFUL MOVEMENT**|**APRAXIA**|\n|**RECOGNITION / FAMILIARITY**|**AGNOSIA**|\n|**VISUOSPATIAL FUNCTION**|**TOPOGRAPHICAL DISORIENTATION**|\n|**SELF-CONTROL / MANAGEMENT**|**EXECUTIVE FUNCTION IMPAIRMENT**|\n\n### Other manifestations — four more\n- **MATHEMATICS —** **ACALCULIA or DYSCALCULIA.**\n- **EMOTIONAL EXPRESSION / COMPREHENSION —** ⚠️ **DEPRESSION IN THE EARLY STAGE, FOLLOWED BY APATHY.**\n- **WRITING —** **AGRAPHIA.**\n- **Behaviour:** **NOT IN ACCORD WITH THE SOCIAL STANDARD OF THE PATIENT.**\n\n### And the exclusion, and the stages\n- **⚠️ The exclusion:** **OTHER CAUSES of dementia or memory loss HAVE TO BE EXCLUDED** — which is what `ge-4`'s treatable list and `ge-10`'s panel are for.\n- **The stages:** **MILD → MODERATE → SEVERE.** **⚠️ The mild stage CAN BE PRECEDED BY A STATE OF \"MILD COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT (MCI)\".**\n- *`ps-symptom` `sy-8` files **recent amnesia** as **the main manifestation in dementia** and as a marker of **organicity**; `sy-9` files **loss of general knowledge and intelligence** in **late dementia**. Neither is repeated here.*\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Alzheimer's disease · Diagnosis of AD · Other manifestations / stages — all in full, every domain and every deficit name",
