        "id": "ge-10",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Investigations, the differential, and pseudo-dementia",
        "body": "### Investigations — three tiers\n|**Tier**|**What the deck lists**|\n|---|---|\n|**COGNITIVE ASSESSMENT**|**MINI-MENTAL STATE EXAMINATION \"MMSE\"** · **MONTREAL COGNITIVE ASSESSMENT \"MoCA\"**|\n|**LAB STUDIES**|**routine chemistry panel** · **SERUM B12 LEVEL** · **THYROID FUNCTION TEST** · **others**|\n|**NEUROIMAGING**|**CT brain or MRI brain, IN CERTAIN CASES**|\n\n- **⚠️ The panel is `ge-4` in reverse:** **B12 finds the nutritional cause, TFT finds hypothyroidism**, and **the imaging finds the chronic subdural haematoma and the normal pressure hydrocephalus.** *The deck never draws that line; it is the reason the panel looks the way it does.*\n- **⚠️ Neuroimaging is qualified — *in certain cases*.** **The deck does not say which**, and none is supplied.\n- *⚠️ **MMSE returns in `nr-delirium`, and there it FAILS:** the delirium half of this same deck states that **the MMSE is NOT SENSITIVE** for it. **The same instrument, opposite verdicts in two halves of one lecture** — and that contrast belongs to both chapters.*\n\n### Differential diagnosis of AD — four\n|**#**|**Differential**|\n|---|---|\n|**1**|**NORMAL FORGETFULNESS OF AGING**|\n|**2**|**OTHER CAUSES OF DEMENTIA** — `ge-5`|\n|**3**|**⚠️ DELIRIUM** — the whole of `nr-delirium`|\n|**4**|**OTHER PSYCHIATRIC ILLNESSES ASSOCIATED WITH MEMORY LOSS**, e.g. **DEPRESSION IN THE ELDERLY**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ PSEUDO-DEMENTIA — the deck's own N.B., and the term to carry:** **sometimes memory loss in elderly depression is obviously present. THIS TYPE OF DEPRESSION IS CALLED PSEUDO-DEMENTIA.**\n- **⚠️ Depression, four roles:** **a risk factor** (`ge-8`), **an early manifestation** of AD itself (`ge-7`), **a differential** here as pseudo-dementia, and **a complication in the caregiver** (`ge-11`). **All four are the deck's; it reconciles none of them.**\n- **⚠️ And no discriminator for differential 2:** **telling AD from the other dementias is what the deck never equips you to do** — `ge-3`'s two BPSD signatures (**visual hallucination → LBD, emotional instability → vascular**) are the only clinical clues printed anywhere in it.\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Investigations of AD · Differential diagnosis of AD — both in full, including the pseudo-dementia N.B.",
