        "body": "### The whole slide\n- **⚠️ The whole slide:** **TO BE A GOOD PSYCHIATRIST YOU HAVE TO BE A GOOD PHYSICIAN.**\n- **BODY — MIND.**\n\n### What that instruction actually requires\n- **⚠️ A two-part examination:** the sheet enforces it three times — **`ps-interview` `iv-5`'s MEDICAL RECORD field is specified as *MENTAL AND PHYSICAL*, and `iv-7`'s family history asks for *OTHER MENTAL AND PHYSICAL ILLNESS*.**\n- **⚠️ Four places give it teeth:**\n  - **`ps-symptom` `sy-9` — ORGANICITY**, *the thread that deck is strung on*: **disorientation, recent amnesia, loss of general knowledge and intelligence** all point away from a primary psychiatric diagnosis.\n  - **`ps-emerg` `em-1`** works a case of **autoimmune encephalitis MIMICKING PSYCHOSIS**, found by **a spinal tap.**\n  - **`ps-schizmgmt` `sm-4`** files **multiple sclerosis, hyperthyroidism, hypothyroidism and the dementias** in the schizophrenia differential.\n  - **`ps-geri` `ge-4`** lists **four TREATABLE dementias** — hypothyroidism, B12 and folate deficiency, normal pressure hydrocephalus, chronic subdural haematoma — **every one found by a physician's investigation, not a psychiatric one.**\n\n### Where this sits in the sheet\n- **Step 1 — HISTORY TAKING:** `ps-interview`, in full.\n- **Step 2 — EXAMINATION:** **this chapter**, `os-2`.\n- **Step 3 — INVESTIGATION:** **this chapter**, `os-3`.\n- *Then `os-4` treatment and `os-5` the AIM, which is the sequence an examiner actually asks a candidate to perform.*\n\nSrc: L1,2 sl. EXAMINATION: — the whole slide is the two lines quoted above. Cross-references to chapters read from disk",
