        "h": "The mental state examination — four blocks, and who teaches each",
        "body": "### The four blocks, as the slide lays them out\n|**Block**|**What it contains**|\n|---|---|\n|**GENERAL LOOK**|ten numbered items — `os-2` below|\n|**BEHAVIOUR**|**abnormal or not** · **ACTIVITY: calm, restless, hyperactive, hypoactive, agitated…**|\n|**AFFECT**|**EMOTIONAL EXPRESSION · APPROPRIATENESS · REACTIVITY**|\n|**INTELLECTUAL FUNCTIONS**|**TOPMAGII** — the eight below|\n\n### GENERAL LOOK — the ten, numbered\n- **The ten, numbered as the slide numbers them:** **1 GENDER · 2 AGE · 3 CONSCIOUSNESS · 4 FACIES · 5 BODY BUILT · 6 CLOTHES · 7 ATTITUDE IN BED OR GAIT · 8 SPECIFIC PATHOLOGICAL FEATURES · 9 EYE CONTACT · 10 COOPERATION.**\n- **⚠️ Item 3 is CONSCIOUSNESS:** **third of ten, before anything psychiatric is assessed at all.** *A patient whose consciousness is not clear is `nr-delirium`, not a psychiatric diagnosis; `ps-geri` `ge-7` makes **CLEAR CONSCIOUSNESS** gate 2 of the Alzheimer's diagnosis for the same reason.*\n- **⚠️ Items 9 and 10:** **eye contact and cooperation are observations of the ENCOUNTER**, not of the patient's body.\n\n### INTELLECTUAL FUNCTIONS — `TOPMAGII`\n|**Letter**|**Function**|**The deck's own detail**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**T**|**THOUGHT & TALK**|**FORM · CONTENT · TYPE**|\n|**O**|**ORIENTATION**|—|\n|**P**|**PERCEPTION**|—|\n|**M**|**MEMORY**|—|\n|**A**|**ATTENTION**|—|\n|**G**|**GENERAL KNOWLEDGE**|—|\n|**I**|**INTELLIGENCE**|—|\n|**I**|**INSIGHT**|—|\n\n### ⚠️ Every one of these is taught in full elsewhere, and this chapter gives the STRUCTURE only\n|**Block**|**Where the content is**|\n|---|---|\n|**AFFECT** — and the four qualitative faults|**`ps-symptom` `sy-3`**, which also defines **la belle indifférence**|\n|**BEHAVIOUR and ACTIVITY** — and catatonia in full|**`ps-symptom` `sy-4`**, which defines **stereotypy**, echolalia and echopraxia|\n|**The TOP-MAGII grid**|**`ps-symptom` `sy-5`**|\n|**T — thought: type, content and form**|**`ps-symptom` `sy-6`**|\n|**P — perception: illusion against hallucination**|**`ps-symptom` `sy-7`**|\n|**O, M, A, G, I, I**|**`ps-symptom` `sy-8`**|\n|**⚠️ ORGANICITY — what an abnormal O, M, G or I actually means**|**`ps-symptom` `sy-9`**|\n\n- **⚠️ Deliberate, and the largest:** **`L4,5` teaches the mental state examination; `L1,2` gives its skeleton.** **Repeating `sy-3` to `sy-9` here would duplicate seven sections.**\n- **⚠️ What `L1,2` adds that `L4,5` does not:** **the GENERAL LOOK block and its ten items** — *`ps-symptom` starts at behaviour and never lists gender, age, facies, body built, clothes, attitude in bed, eye contact or cooperation.* **That block is this chapter's own contribution.**\n\nSrc: L1,2 sl. MENTAL STATE EXAMINATION, in full — all four blocks, all ten General Look items, all eight TOPMAGII letters. The content column is `ps-symptom`, read from disk section by section",
