        "h": "Investigations — four modalities, four reasons, and no specific test",
        "body": "### The four modalities\n- **The four:** **LABORATORY · IMAGING · NEUROPHYSIOLOGY · PSYCHOMETRY.**\n\n### ⚠️ The question the slide asks, and answers by implication\n- **⚠️ The deck's question:** **\"IS THERE A SPECIFIC TEST FOR PSYCHIATRIC ILLNESS?\"** — **and it then prints \"SO WHY?\", which only makes sense if the answer is NO.**\n- *`ps-anxiety` `ax-6` states it outright from `L4,5`: **\"NO DIAGNOSTIC TEST\".*** **Same claim, one deck stating it and one implying it.**\n\n### So why order them — the four reasons\n|**#**|**Reason**|**Where the module shows it working**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1**|**DIAGNOSTIC, or for DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS**|**`ps-geri` `ge-10`** — serum B12 and thyroid function find two of the four **treatable** dementias|\n|**2**|**SEARCH FOR AETIOLOGY AND/OR COMPLICATIONS**|**`ps-emerg` `em-1`** — the spinal tap that found **anti-NMDA receptor antibodies** behind an apparent psychosis|\n|**3**|**TREATMENT CHOICE, or FOLLOW-UP**|**`ps-pharm`** — and **`ps-geri` `ge-11`**, where the cholinesterase inhibitors and memantine are chosen **by stage**|\n|**4**|**⚠️ LEGAL**|⚠️ **and the module teaches nothing about it.** *`ps-somato` `so-10` names the **medicolegal and forensic populations** as where malingering is met, and `ps-interview` `iv-8` records that **FORENSIC HISTORY is listed on this same sheet and given no slide.* **Three mentions of the legal dimension, no teaching on any of them.***\n\n- **⚠️ Two modalities, one place each:** **NEUROPHYSIOLOGY** is **EEG** in `nr-epilepsy` and `ps-emerg` `em-7` (**non-convulsive status epilepticus in an unresponsive patient**); **PSYCHOMETRY** is **QEEG brain mapping** in `ps-devices` `dv-9` / `ps-child` `ch-10`. **No psychometric instrument is named anywhere in this deck** — *`ps-geri` `ge-10`'s **MMSE** and **MoCA** and `ps-ocd` `oc-7`'s **Y-BOCS** are the module's only three, and all come from other lectures.*\n\nSrc: L1,2 sl. Investigations, in full — the four modalities, the question and all four reasons",
