        "body": "### The four steps, as the closing slide prints them\n|**Step**|**What it is**|**Where it is taught**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**1 — PATIENT ASSESSMENT**|**HISTORY TAKING · MENTAL STATE EXAMINATION · ⚠️ RISK ASSESSMENT**|`ps-interview` · `os-2` · ⚠️ **risk assessment: see below**|\n|**2 — FORMULATION OF THE CASE**|⚠️ **named and never defined**|**nowhere** — see below|\n|**3 — RECOMMEND FURTHER PSYCHOMETRIC TEST AND INVESTIGATIONS**|the four modalities and four reasons|`os-3`|\n|**4 — TREATMENT: BIOPSYCHOSOCIAL APPROACH**|the four tools|`os-4`|\n\n- **⚠️ THIS SLIDE IS THE STATION.** *An examiner who asks a candidate to \"assess this patient\" is asking for exactly these four steps in this order — which is why this chapter, and not `ps-symptom`, is the one to read before an OSCE.*\n\n### ⚠️ Two of the four steps name something the module never teaches\n- **RISK ASSESSMENT —** **named here as one of the three parts of patient assessment, and taught nowhere as a procedure.** *`ps-emerg` `em-3` gives **three causes, ten risk factors** for suicide and **`em-1`** the three ways an emergency is missed; **that is the nearest the module comes, and it is a risk-factor list, not an assessment method.*** **No structured tool, no question set, no documentation standard appears in any deck.**\n- **FORMULATION OF THE CASE —** ⚠️⚠️ **`formulation` returns hits in this deck alone across all 25 caches, and this slide is the only one.** **The deck names the single most examined skill in a psychiatric OSCE and never says what a formulation contains.** *It is conventionally the summary that draws history, mental state and background into one explanatory account — predisposing, precipitating, perpetuating and protective factors* **(not taken from the course material)**. **Nothing further is supplied: a formulation model written from memory is not a gap-fill.**\n\n- **⚠️ What the candidate DOES have, in full:** the **seven parts of the history** (`ps-interview`), the **four rules for recording a complaint**, the **ten complaint domains** (`ps-symptom` `sy-2`), the **four MSE blocks** with **General Look's ten items** and **TOPMAGII** (`os-2`), the **four investigation modalities and four reasons** (`os-3`), and the **four treatment tools** (`os-4`).\n\nSrc: L1,2 sl. AIM, in full — all four steps and all three parts of step 1. The formulation gloss is tagged; the `formulation` probe was run over all 25 caches",
