        "body": "### ⚠️⚠️ Where the demonstration actually is — and it is not in the text corpus\n- **The probe that started the worry:** **this chapter is titled *OSCE demonstration*, and `OSCE` returns ZERO across all 25 cached decks.**\n- **⚠️ And the probe was wrong:** **it searched the examiner's word, not the source's.** **`L1,2) Psychiatric sheet` IS the OSCE task** — sixteen text slides of clerking framework, split at its own `EXAMINATION:` slide into `ps-interview` and this chapter. *The third time this module has paid for probing in the question's vocabulary rather than the source's — after `ps-anxiety`'s **GAD** and `nr-intro`'s **lateral column**.*\n- **⚠️ Outside the text:** **the book's two OSCE-shaped contents rows — `Psychiatric Sheet` and `Clinical Case` — are QR VIDEO LINKS WITH NO PAGE NUMBER.** *The framework is printed; **the demonstration is a video, and no page of any source carries it.*** **Recorded, not treated as a gap in the text.**\n\n### The seam\n- **`ps-interview` is slides 1–11** — the history. **This chapter is slides 12–16** — examination, investigations, treatment, aim. **The break is the deck's own `EXAMINATION:` slide: CONTIGUOUS, nothing reordered.**\n\n### What this chapter POINTS at rather than repeating\n|**Content**|**Lives in**|**Verified?**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Affect and its four qualitative faults**|`ps-symptom` `sy-3`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Behaviour, activity, catatonia, stereotypy**|`ps-symptom` `sy-4`|✅ read from disk|\n|**The TOP-MAGII grid**, and T, P, and O/M/A/G/I/I in full|`ps-symptom` `sy-5` to `sy-8`|✅ read from disk|\n|**ORGANICITY — what an abnormal O, M, G or I means**|`ps-symptom` `sy-9`|✅ read from disk|\n|**\"NO DIAGNOSTIC TEST\", stated outright**|`ps-anxiety` `ax-6`|✅ read from disk|\n|**The four treatment arms, against L18's four**|`ps-therapy` `th-1`|✅ **already prints this deck's list**|\n|**Psychotherapy · psychopharmacology · devices**|`ps-therapy` · `ps-pharm` · `ps-devices`|✅ written|\n|**EEG in an unresponsive patient · QEEG brain mapping**|`ps-emerg` `em-7` · `ps-devices` `dv-9`|✅ read from disk|\n\n### ⚠️ Verified absences — probed across all 25 cached decks\n|**What**|**Probe result**|\n|---|---|\n|**`OSCE`**|**ZERO.** The word is the app's, not the syllabus's. **The task is taught; the label is not**|\n|**`formulation`**|**⚠️⚠️ THIS DECK ALONE, on the AIM slide.** **The single most examined skill in a psychiatric OSCE is NAMED and never defined.** Glossed and **tagged** in `os-5`; nothing further supplied|\n|**RISK ASSESSMENT as a method**|**named in the AIM slide and taught nowhere as a procedure.** `risk assessment` returns **one further hit — inside an `L16` case narrative**, *\"formal Suicide Risk Assessment was performed\"*, which **names it without describing it.** `ps-emerg` `em-3`'s **three causes and ten risk factors** are the nearest the module comes, and **a risk-factor list is not an assessment method**|\n|**HOSPITALIZATION as a procedure**|⚠️⚠️ **NOT an absence, and the probe nearly recorded one.** `hospitali[sz]` hits **eight decks**; the hits were **OPENED**, and four are real teaching — **`ps-mood` `mo-8`'s four indications**, **`ps-schizmgmt` `sm-5`**, **`ps-anxiety` `ax-9`**, **`ps-emerg` `em-7`**. **The tool this slide names is taught in full, elsewhere** (`os-4`). *The sixteenth payment of **open the hit before explaining it away.***|\n|**PSYCHOMETRY — any named instrument**|**none in this deck.** The module's only three — **MMSE**, **MoCA** (`ps-geri` `ge-10`) and **Y-BOCS** (`ps-ocd` `oc-7`) — **all come from other lectures**|\n|**A WORKED EXAMPLE — specimen history, model formulation, mark scheme, station**|**none anywhere.** ⚠️ **The deck gives the framework and never fills it in**|\n|**CONSENT and CAPACITY**|**⚠️ `ps-therapy` `th-11` already records that NO CONSENT PROCEDURE IS TAUGHT ANYWHERE in the module** — one hit, on its ethics slide. **Nothing here changes that**|\n\n### ⚠️ One source is UNREAD, and this is recorded rather than guessed\n- **Book Psychiatry ch.1**, which the book map records as carrying **genuine mental-state-examination technique at printed p.184.** **Image-only and unread**; a render was not authorised for this chapter. ⚠️ **It is `ps-symptom`'s chapter and `ps-interview`'s before it is this one's**, and the plan records that reading it here would be **reading it a third time.**\n\nSrc: register verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js read from disk, section by section. Absence probes over all 25 caches in content/neuro/lectures/. The QR-video finding is from content/neuro/book-map.md",
