        "h": "Aetiology — systemic illness, at two grains",
        "body": "### ⚠️ The framing clause\n- **IT IS USUALLY MULTIFACTORIAL.** *So the search does not stop at the first cause found.*\n\n### A — Systemic illness, the deck's nine groups\n|**Group**|**Examples printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**INFECTIONS**|—|\n|**ELECTROLYTE ABNORMALITIES**|—|\n|**ENDOCRINE DYSFUNCTIONS**|**hypo- OR hyper-**|\n|**LIVER FAILURE**|**HEPATIC ENCEPHALOPATHY**|\n|**RENAL FAILURE**|**URAEMIC ENCEPHALOPATHY**|\n|**PULMONARY DISEASE**|**with HYPOXAEMIA**|\n|**CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE / EVENTS**|**CHF · ARRHYTHMIAS · MI**|\n|**CNS PATHOLOGY**|**TUMOURS · STROKES · SEIZURES**|\n|**DEFICIENCY STATES**|**THIAMINE · NICOTINIC ACID · FOLIC ACID · B12**|\n\n### ⚠️ The book prints the same list as the causes of TOXIC-METABOLIC COMA, in four groups\n*Book Neurology ch.11, printed p.101 — **the same aetiology, one stage further along.***\n\n|**Book group**|**What it adds that L13 does not print**|\n|---|---|\n|**1 — Deprivation of oxygen, substrate or cofactor (shock)**|**HYPOXIA · DIFFUSE ISCHAEMIA · any cause of HYPOTENSION** · **HYPOGLYCAEMIA** · **thiamine deficiency named as WERNICKE–KORSAKOFF SYNDROME**|\n|**2 — Disease of organs other than brain**|**LUNG — CO₂ NARCOSIS** · **PANCREAS — diabetes, hypoglycaemia** · **THYROID — MYXOEDEMA, THYROTOXICOSIS** · **ADRENAL — ADDISON, CUSHING, PHAEOCHROMOCYTOMA** · **SEPSIS**|\n|**3 — Exogenous poisons**|**sedatives and narcotics · psychotropic drugs · ACID POISONS (methyl alcohol, ethylene glycol) · anticonvulsants · HEAVY METALS · CYANIDE**|\n|**4 — Abnormalities of electrolytes**|**named individually: SODIUM (hypo- and hyper-), ACIDOSIS, ALKALOSIS, MAGNESIUM, CALCIUM, PHOSPHORUS**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ THE TWO SOURCES DO NOT DISAGREE — THEY DIFFER IN GRAIN.** **L13 names the organ; the book names the mechanism and the specific derangement.** *Both are transcribed; neither is corrected.*\n- **⚠️ Hypoglycaemia:** **on the book's list and NOT on L13's** — and **`nr-coma` records it as the one metabolic cause the book says to treat before anything else.**\n- *⚠️ **THIAMINE, third time in this module.** `ps-geri` `ge-5` has it as a **nutritional** cause of dementia — *thiamine deficiency, \"Wernicke Korsakoff psychosis\"* — and `ps-sud` `sd-8` records that **Wernicke is never taught as an alcohol-withdrawal syndrome anywhere.** **The book's p.101 line is the third naming and it too gives no triad and no treatment.** **The hole `sd-8` names is still open.***\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Etiology, in full — all nine systemic groups · book Neurology ch.11 printed p.101, the four causal groups of metabolic coma in full",
