        "body": "### ⚠️ The framing clause, and it is a wide one\n- **The framing clause, and it is wide:** **ANY PSYCHOACTIVE MEDICATION CAN CAUSE DELIRIUM.** *So the list below is illustrative, not exhaustive — and the deck says so.*\n- **Three mechanisms, all three named:** **TOXICITY · WITHDRAWAL · SIDE EFFECTS of these medications.**\n\n### The twelve classes\n|**Class**|**Agents printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**⚠️ ANTICHOLINERGICS**|**as TCAs**|\n|**ANALGESICS**|**MORPHINE · CODEINE**|\n|**STEROIDS**|—|\n|**ANTIPARKINSONIAN**|**anticholinergic AND dopaminergic**|\n|**SEDATIVES**|**BENZODIAZEPINES · BARBITURATES** · **ALCOHOL**|\n|**ANTICONVULSANTS**|—|\n|**ANTIHISTAMINES**|—|\n|**ANTIARRHYTHMICS**|**DIGITALIS**|\n|**ANTIHYPERTENSIVES**|—|\n|**ANTIDEPRESSANTS**|—|\n|**ANTIMICROBIALS**|**PENICILLIN · CEPHALOSPORINS · QUINOLONES**|\n|**SYMPATHOMIMETICS**|—|\n|**OTHERS**|**FUROSEMIDE · DIGOXIN · THEOPHYLLINE · CIMETIDINE · CAPTOPRIL**|\n\n- **⚠️ Anticholinergic burden runs through it:** named as a class, again under antiparkinsonian, **and TCAs and antihistamines carry it too.** *That is why `dl-9`'s treatment says to **minimise psychoactive medications, especially those with anticholinergic potential.***\n- **⚠️ It is other chapters' treatment list:** **benzodiazepines are `ps-anxiety`'s; antidepressants and antipsychotics are `ps-pharm`'s; anticonvulsants are `nr-epilepsy`'s; steroids appear in `nr-cns`, `ps-geri` and `nr-ms`.** *A drug that treats one chapter's disease causes this one's.*\n- *⚠️ **The book adds a class L13 does not:** **NARCOTIC and BENZODIAZEPINE OVERDOSE**, with **IV NALOXONE or FLUMAZENIL** as the response in a comatose patient without focal findings (`nr-coma`). **L13 names no antidote for any of its twelve classes.***\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Etiology — Medications, in full including every named agent · the naloxone/flumazenil line is book Neurology ch.11 printed p.117, via `nr-coma`",
