        "body": "### ⚠️⚠️ The MMSE fails here — and the same deck relies on it for dementia\n- **The finding:** **THE MINI-MENTAL STATE EXAMINATION IS NOT SENSITIVE IN IDENTIFYING DELIRIUM.**\n- **⚠️ But serially it works:** **REPEATED MMSEs CAN REVEAL THE WAXING AND WANING COURSE.** *The instrument is useless once and useful repeated — because **fluctuation is the hallmark** (`dl-1`), and a single score cannot show fluctuation.*\n- **⚠️⚠️ Opposite verdicts, one lecture:** **`ps-geri` `ge-10` lists the MMSE and MoCA as the cognitive assessment for dementia, from the FIRST HALF OF THIS SAME DECK.** *Both are transcribed; the deck never sets them against each other.*\n\n### The three most sensitive items\n- **SERIAL 7s · ORIENTATION · RECALL MEMORY.**\n\n### Tests of attention — four, and the deck names them\n|**Test**|\n|---|\n|**SERIAL 7s**|\n|**SPELLING `WORLD` BACKWARDS**|\n|**MONTHS OF THE YEAR BACKWARD**|\n|**COUNTING DOWN FROM 20**|\n\n- **⚠️ SERIAL 7s IS ON BOTH LISTS** — it is both a sensitive MMSE item and a test of attention, **which is why it is the single most useful bedside task in a suspected delirium.**\n- **⚠️ All four are reversed or serial:** they work because they need attention to be **SUSTAINED AND MANIPULATED**, not merely present — which is characteristic 3 of `dl-5`.\n- *⚠️ **No score, cut-off or administration instruction is printed for the MMSE anywhere in either half of this deck**, and `ps-geri` `ge-12` records the same. **`ps-ocd` `oc-7`'s Y-BOCS is the module's only other named instrument.***\n\n### What the book adds — the one test that settles it\n- **⚠️ EEG.** Book Neurology ch.11 gives it for the comatose patient: **it can DISTINGUISH COMA FROM PSYCHIC UNRESPONSIVENESS AND LOCKED-IN STATE**, is **ALWAYS ABNORMAL IN TRUE COMA**, and **may reveal clinically unsuspected seizure activity.** *`nr-coma` carries it in full.*\n- **⚠️ No investigation at all:** **L13 names none for delirium** — **no bloods, no imaging, no EEG.** *Its testing slide is bedside cognitive tasks and nothing else, even though characteristic 7 of `dl-5` requires **evidence from history, physical examination OR LABS.*** **The labs it demands are not listed.** *`nr-coma` prints the panel; **this deck does not.***\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Testing, in full · book Neurology ch.11 printed p.116 for the EEG line, via `nr-coma`",
