        "body": "### 1 — Treat the underlying cause\n- **TREAT THE UNDERLYING CAUSE.** *First line, and `dl-6` explains why: **symptoms continue to progress or fluctuate UNTIL the underlying cause is treated.** No drug below shortens that.*\n\n### 2 — Environmental interventions, and the deck lists them in detail\n|**Intervention**|**Detail printed**|\n|---|---|\n|**CUES FOR ORIENTATION**|**CALENDAR · CLOCK · FAMILY PICTURES · WINDOWS**|\n|**REORIENT the patient**|**FREQUENTLY**|\n|**VISITORS**|**family or friends visit FREQUENTLY** — ⚠️ **making sure they INTRODUCE THEMSELVES**|\n|**STAFF**|**MINIMIZE STAFF SWITCHING**|\n\n- **⚠️ All four attack one problem:** **the patient cannot hold new information.** *A window and a clock supply orientation externally; an introduction supplies identity; one nurse instead of six reduces how much must be re-learned.*\n- **⚠️ The only drug-free measures:** and **they come first.** *`ps-geri` `ge-11` gives the dementia equivalent — **environmental modification and attention to safety** — from the same lecture.*\n\n### 3 — Subtract before you add\n- **MINIMIZE PSYCHOACTIVE MEDICATIONS**, **ESPECIALLY THOSE WITH ANTICHOLINERGIC POTENTIAL and SEDATING ONES.**\n- **⚠️ This is `dl-4` run backwards** — the twelve classes that cause delirium are the first thing to stop.\n\n### 4 — Drugs, and only for one indication\n|**Drug**|**What the deck says**|\n|---|---|\n|**HALOPERIDOL**|**SMALL DOSES of antipsychotics** *\"as haloperidol\"*|\n|**RISPERIDONE**|**same clause** — small doses|\n|**QUETIAPINE**|**ATYPICAL antipsychotics MAY be used, as LOW DOSES of quetiapine**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ The indication is narrow:** **TO CONTROL AGITATION**, and the deck states it. *So drugs are for the **hyperactive** subtype of `dl-5`. **Nothing at all is offered for the hypoactive subtype** — the one `dl-5` flags as most easily missed.*\n- **⚠️ NOT ONE DOSE IS PRINTED.** **\"Small doses\" and \"low doses\" are the whole quantification** for all three agents. **Deliberately not supplied** — an antipsychotic dose in a delirious, medically ill patient written from memory is exactly what this project's citation rule forbids.\n- *⚠️ **The same two agents, in their own indication, are `ps-schizmgmt`'s; `ps-geri` `ge-11` names risperidone and haloperidol for BPSD with the identical hedge** — **cautiously, lowest possible dose, to prevent sedation.*** **Two halves of one lecture, one prescribing rule.**\n- **⚠️ NO BENZODIAZEPINE is offered**, although **benzodiazepines and alcohol are on `dl-4`'s causal list** — *and withdrawal from them is one of the three named mechanisms.* **The deck names no treatment for withdrawal delirium specifically**, and `ps-sud` `sd-8` records that **no intoxication or withdrawal syndrome is taught anywhere in the module.**\n\nSrc: L13 sl. Treatment, in full — all four arms and all three named agents",
