        "body": "### Consciousness — and it has two components, not one\n- **The definition:** **AWARENESS OF SELF AND ENVIRONMENT.** It **requires BOTH AROUSAL AND MENTAL CONTENT**, and **the integrity of the RETICULAR ACTIVATING SYSTEM AND THE CEREBRAL CORTEX.**\n\n|**Component**|**What it is**|**What it depends on**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**CONTENT**|**the SUM of COGNITIVE AND AFFECTIVE FUNCTION**|**BOTH cerebral cortices**|\n|**AROUSAL**|**the APPEARANCE OF WAKEFULNESS**|**the ASCENDING RETICULAR ACTIVATING SYSTEM**|\n\n### ⚠️⚠️ The asymmetry that organises the whole chapter\n- **The asymmetry:** **THE CONTENT DEPENDS ON AROUSAL, BUT NORMAL AROUSAL DOES NOT GUARANTEE NORMAL CONTENT.**\n\n|**What is damaged**|**What results**|\n|---|---|\n|**AROUSAL**|**COMA · SEMI-COMA · DELIRIUM**|\n|**CONTENT**|**DEMENTIA · DELUSIONS · CONFUSION · INATTENTION**|\n\n- **⚠️ It places four chapters:** **`nr-delirium` and this chapter are AROUSAL failures; `ps-geri`'s dementia and `ps-psychosis`'s delusions are CONTENT failures.** *The book states it in two lines and the decks never state it at all.*\n- **⚠️ And it explains the direction of travel:** **a patient can lose content and stay awake — that is dementia.** **A patient cannot lose arousal and keep content** — which is why **`ps-geri` `ge-7` makes CLEAR CONSCIOUSNESS a diagnostic gate for Alzheimer's**, and why **`ps-osce` `os-2` puts CONSCIOUSNESS third of ten in the General Look, before anything psychiatric.**\n- **⚠️ The one exception:** **`co-8`'s LOCKED-IN SYNDROME**, where **arousal and content are BOTH intact and only the output is gone.**\n\nSrc: book Neurology ch.11 printed p.99, in full — the definition, both components and the damage table",
