        "id": "co-4",
        "w": "must",
        "h": "Toxic-metabolic coma — two thirds, and how it announces itself",
        "body": "### The share\n- **⚠️ The share:** **TOXIC-METABOLIC COMA IS TWO THIRDS OF ALL CASES.** *Structural is the other third (`co-6`), and psychiatric causes are a residue (`co-7`).*\n\n### The six differentiating features\n|**#**|**Feature**|\n|---|---|\n|**1**|**⚠️ CONFUSION AND STUPOR COMMONLY PRECEDE MOTOR SIGNS** — *a confusional state or **DELIRIUM occurs initially*** |\n|**2**|**MOTOR SIGNS ARE USUALLY SYMMETRICAL**|\n|**3**|**⚠️ PUPILLARY REACTIONS ARE USUALLY PRESERVED**|\n|**4**|**ASTERIXIS, MYOCLONUS, TREMOR AND SEIZURES ARE COMMON**|\n|**5**|**ACID-BASE IMBALANCE with HYPER- or HYPOVENTILATION is FREQUENT**|\n|**6**|**TREMULOUSNESS, MYOCLONIC JERKS AND ASTERIXIS ARE TYPICAL**|\n\n- **⚠️⚠️ Feature 1 is a bridge:** **a metabolic coma is a delirium that did not stop**, and **a delirium is a metabolic encephalopathy that has not yet reached coma.** *`nr-delirium` teaches the first stage and the book the second; **neither says they are the same process**, and this line is where they meet.*\n- **⚠️ Two findings decide it:** **SYMMETRY and REACTIVE PUPILS point metabolic; asymmetry and a fixed pupil point structural** (`co-6`).\n- **⚠️ The infographic agrees:** **symmetrical motor signs — tremors, asterixis and myoclonus affect BOTH SIDES EQUALLY** · **preserved pupillary reactions — UNLIKE STRUCTURAL DAMAGE** · **a preceding confusional state.** **Common causes it names: ORGAN FAILURE (liver/kidney), DRUG TOXINS, ELECTROLYTE IMBALANCES.**\n\nSrc: book Neurology ch.11 printed p.100 (the six differentiating features) and p.103 (the two-column infographic), both in full",
