        "h": "The four causal groups of metabolic coma",
        "body": "### 1 — Deprivation of oxygen, substrate or metabolic cofactor (shock)\n- **HYPOXIA · DIFFUSE ISCHAEMIA** — **cardiac disease · decreased peripheral circulatory resistance · increased cerebrovascular resistance · widespread small-vessel occlusion** — **or ANY CAUSE OF HYPOTENSION.**\n- **⚠️ HYPOGLYCAEMIA.** *`nr-comapproach` `ca-1` records that the book treats it empirically before waiting for anything.*\n- **⚠️ THIAMINE DEFICIENCY — WERNICKE–KORSAKOFF SYNDROME.**\n\n### 2 — Disease of organs other than the brain\n|**Organ**|**What it produces**|\n|---|---|\n|**LIVER**|**HEPATIC COMA · SEDATIVE HYPERSENSITIVITY**|\n|**KIDNEY**|**URAEMIA**|\n|**LUNG**|**CO₂ NARCOSIS**|\n|**PANCREAS**|**DIABETES · HYPOGLYCAEMIA · EXOCRINE PANCREATIC ENCEPHALOPATHY**|\n|**THYROID**|**MYXOEDEMA · THYROTOXICOSIS**|\n|**ADRENAL**|**ADDISON or CUSHING DISEASE · PHAEOCHROMOCYTOMA**|\n|**Other systemic disease**|**e.g. SEPSIS**|\n\n### 3 — Exogenous poisons (drugs or toxins)\n- **The six named:** **SEDATIVES AND NARCOTICS · PSYCHOTROPIC DRUGS · ACID POISONS (METHYL ALCOHOL, ETHYLENE GLYCOL) · ANTICONVULSANTS · HEAVY METALS · CYANIDE.**\n\n### 4 — Abnormalities of electrolytes\n- **WATER AND SODIUM — HYPO- and HYPERNATRAEMIA · ACIDOSIS · ALKALOSIS · MAGNESIUM, hyper- and hypo- · CALCIUM, hyper- and hypo- · PHOSPHORUS — HYPOPHOSPHATAEMIA.**\n\n### ⚠️ Where this list has already been seen\n- **⚠️⚠️ The same aetiology, coarser:** **`nr-delirium` `dl-3` prints it as organs — infections, electrolytes, endocrine, liver, renal, pulmonary, cardiovascular, CNS, deficiency states.** **The book names the mechanism and the specific derangement.** *The two do not disagree; **they differ in grain**, and both are transcribed.*\n- **⚠️ Thiamine, a fourth time:** and **still without a triad.** `ps-geri` `ge-5` has it as a nutritional dementia; `nr-delirium` `dl-3` as a deficiency state; **`ps-sud` `sd-8` records that Wernicke is NEVER taught as an alcohol-withdrawal syndrome anywhere.** **This page names the syndrome and gives no features and no treatment.** ✅ *But `nr-comapproach` `ca-1` gives the **dose**: **IV thiamine, at least 100 mg**, with the empirical dextrose — **the module's only quantified thiamine.***\n\nSrc: book Neurology ch.11 printed p.101, in full — all four causal groups and every example",
