        "body": "### ⚠️⚠️ The split — this chapter is half of a book chapter, and the other half is `nr-comapproach`\n- **The arithmetic:** **book Neurology ch.11 is ONE chapter of twenty printed pages.** **Written whole it measured 6,543 words**, and **at every words-per-page rate this module has recorded — 296 to 391 — that is 17 to 22 printed pages.** **There is no rate at which it fits the ≤13-page shape.**\n- **⚠️ Measured, not forecast:** **the split rests on a written word count**, and **the seam is the book's own banner — `APPROACH TO THE PATIENT IN COMA`, printed p.106.** **Contiguous, nothing reordered.**\n- **This chapter is printed 99–106: what coma IS, and what mimics it.** **`nr-comapproach` is printed 106–118: what to DO about it** — golden rules, history, examination, the Glasgow Coma Scale, investigation, management and prognosis.\n- **⚠️ And `nr-delirium` is the third piece.** *The declared chapter was **Delirium and Coma**; the deck taught delirium and the book taught coma, so **the delirium half went to `nr-delirium` and coma became these two.*** **`SCHEDULE` is keyed by date and title and is untouched.**\n\n### What this chapter hands on\n|**Fact**|**Goes to**|\n|---|---|\n|**The GLASGOW COMA SCALE**, every row and the severity bands|**`nr-comapproach` `ca-3`**|\n|**The pupils, eye movements and the conjugate gaze pathway**|**`nr-comapproach` `ca-4`**|\n|**Respiratory patterns, posturing and herniation**|**`nr-comapproach` `ca-5`**|\n|**Investigation, and management in three situations**|**`nr-comapproach` `ca-6`**|\n|**PROGNOSIS, and the book's two unanswered questions worked**|**`nr-comapproach` `ca-7`**|\n\n### What this chapter POINTS at rather than repeating\n|**Fact**|**Lives in**|**Verified?**|\n|---|---|---|\n|**DELIRIUM in full** — six names, three motor subtypes, the dementia table|`nr-delirium`|✅ read from disk|\n|**DEMENTIA**, the content failure of `co-1`'s table|`ps-geri`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Meningitis, both meningeal signs, the meningococcal rash**|`nr-cns` `ci-2`, `ci-5`|✅ read from disk|\n|**CATATONIA in full, and why it needs an EEG**|`ps-emerg` `em-7`|✅ read from disk|\n|**Status epilepticus and its protocol**|`nr-epilepsy` `ep-10`|✅ read from disk|\n|**The thalamus as the sensory relay**|`nr-intro`|✅ written|\n|**CLEAR CONSCIOUSNESS as a diagnostic gate**|`ps-geri` `ge-7` · `ps-osce` `os-2`|✅ read from disk|\n\n### ⚠️ What is absent, recorded not guessed\n- **THALAMIC LESIONS** — **on the book's own six-item coma differential (`co-7`) and never expanded anywhere in the chapter.**\n- **⚠️⚠️ NO DECK TEACHES ANY OF THIS.** **`Glasgow`, `GCS` and `brain death` return ZERO across all 25 cached decks**, and **`coma` appears only as a passing mention in four.** **This chapter exists because the book was rendered and read.**\n\n### The source, and do not re-read it\n- **The source:** **book Neurology ch.11, `CLINICAL APPROACH TO \"COMA\" CASE` — printed 99–118 = PDF 110–129, TWENTY pages, 5,374 words.** **Rendered at 150 dpi and read by two subagents on 2026-08-23**, on the user's explicit authorisation, and **cached to `content/neuro/book/` as `neuro-ch11-coma-a.txt` and `neuro-ch11-coma-b.txt`.** ⚠️ **The `+11` offset was verified footer by footer on all twenty pages. Nothing was illegible.** ⚠️⚠️ **DO NOT RE-RENDER.**\n- **⚠️ Both boundaries were read:** **the chapter begins on printed p.99 with its `CHAPTER 11` banner** and ends on p.118. **Neither was inferred.**\n\nSrc: the split record and register verified against app/data/theory.neuro.js read from disk. Source provenance from content/neuro/book/ and content/neuro/book-map.md",
